Phnom Penh Governor Urges Acceleration of Boeung Trabek Canal to Reduce Flooding in Rainy Season
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, urged the working group of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh and the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Phnom Penh to speed up the restoration of Boeung Trabek Canal to open the waterway quickly. Boeung Trabek station so that this station can pump water out quickly, reduce the flooding of people's houses in this rainy season.
Mr. Khuong Sreng's urging took place on the afternoon of July 5, 2022, as he led professional officials such as Chamkar Mon District Authority to inspect the restoration of Boeung Trabek, which is approximately one kilometer from Boeung Trabek Canal to the station. Boeung Trabek, Street 271.
Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed the team of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh as well as the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Phnom Penh to remove garbage, mud and grass, which is a barrier in the Boeung Trabek canal, when it rains heavily. It can flow quickly to the front of the station, which allows the Boeung Trabek station to be able to pump water quickly, reducing the flooding of people's homes in the rainy season.
According to the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration, the Boeung Trabek Canal was urged by Mr. Khuong Sreng to be rehabilitated with the construction of a 10-meter-wide and 827-meter-long dam at the mouth of the canal.
