Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor Brings Vesa Candles and Gifts to Monks at Wat Seila Rainsy (Wat Thkov) and Wat Vihear Tontum
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan and his wife, as well as their sons, are devout Buddhists who regularly bring candles and offerings to monks at temples every year for three months.
The ceremony of offering Preah Vossa candles, suffixes and offerings was made in accordance with the Buddhist scriptures, including blessings and blessings for Dr. and Mrs. and their children, as well as provincial leaders and government officials who were invited to attend.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan paid a courtesy call and called on the people to continue to work together with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to protect the achievements of the Royal Government in the field of Buddhism and special empire. Peace can be achieved at all costs, that is, "without peace, there would be no development like today."
The meaningful ceremony was held on the morning of July 5, 2022 under the presidency of Dr. Hun Manet, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, after four traditional Buddhist ceremonies. 5 nights already.
Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, confirmed that the Bun Seangly Heritage Temple is another great achievement that comes from the legacy and wisdom of the Duke of the Supreme Disciple Vivathana Bun Seangly, the mother of Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. Come and lead and build the Buddhist temple in Wat Sleng 8 years ago.
He stressed that under all circumstances, Samdech Techo Hun Sen never fled the people and left any people to suffer. With the efforts of the people to find 19 vaccines against Kovid, vaccinated to Cambodians and foreigners free of charge and vaccinated more than 90% of Cambodians across the country.
In addition, Dr. HUN Manet appealed to the people in Takeo province, especially the people of Kirivong district, to participate in the 3rd, 4th and 5th vaccinations for all Cambodians. Out of the deadly disease Kovid 19.
Please note that Wat Sleng is one of the ancient pagodas in Kirivong district, Takeo province, more than 300 years old, 150 meters wide and 240 meters long, located in Sleng village, Kork Prech commune, Kirivong district, Takeo province. .
Wat Sleng is one of the oldest monasteries in Kirivong district, built in the late 16th century AD 1622, according to inscriptions on ancient stupas and artifacts such as Prak Duong. And the old stone pillars found in the ancient temple canyons buried by the ancestors of that generation, as well as living documents from the elders at the same time.
The reason why it is called Wat Sleng is because this pagoda was built on the top of a mountain called Phnom Jing Chak and this mountain is rich in big Sleng trees, so the Chief Inspector and the elders who are the founders of this pagoda first agreed to name Wat Sleng From then until now.
Since its inception, this ancient monastery has been visited by many chief priests, but since the days of the liberation on January 7, 1979, Wat Sleng monasteries as well as other monasteries across the country have reopened to practice their religious beliefs. As well as the survival of the country and the people of Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, instructed the newly elected Sangkat Councilors of Sangkat O Smach and Sangkat Samrong to fulfill their special duties and responsibilities in providing public services to the people with high responsibility.
This statement was made on the occasion that he validated the members of Sangkat O Smach and Sangkat Samrong on the morning of July 5, 2022. On that occasion, the Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province stated that since 2002, the Kingdom of Cambodia has organized a total of 5 Commune / Sangkat Council elections in accordance with the principles of liberal multi-party democracy.
Elections to establish councils at the commune level have a profound effect on Cambodia's political and administrative system:
Mr. Pen Kosal said that the election of councils at the commune level is very important to accelerate the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration reforms in the sub-national administration, which has played an important role in promoting governance. At the commune level, according to the principles of democratic development at the local level.
