Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor pays a courtesy call on a Royal Thai Navy delegation visiting Cambodia
He said that today is the mission of the Royal Thai Navy to send a ship to visit Cambodia for the first time after the disease has been cured. Despite the effects of Kovid, the two navies held a series of remote meetings online.
In response, Kouch Chamroeun welcomed a Royal Thai Navy delegation from Thailand to visit Cambodia for the first time after the Kovid-19 outbreak two years ago.
Cambodia has also received nine Royal Thai Navy ships, equivalent to 13 ships, docked at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, and this visit is to strengthen the bonds of solidarity, friendship and cooperation between the navies of Cambodia. Both countries are getting stronger. Cambodia and Thailand are countries in the same ASEAN region, and this year Cambodia will also chair the ASEAN Summit.
The provincial governor said that although in 2020, Cambodia as well as the world was in the fight against Kovid-19, but the fight against drugs across the border, Cambodia and Thailand have cooperated well by collecting packages. There is a lot of drug abuse in the open sea, and this result reflects the actions of criminals who have not had the opportunity to smuggle drugs.
During the visit of the Royal Thai Navy now and shared the experience between the navies of both countries, Cambodia and the Royal Thai Navy. We are a country in the same ASEAN region, with Thais coming to work in Sihanoukville and a large number of Cambodians going to work in Thailand.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun wished the visit and excursion of the Royal Thai Navy delegation in Sihanoukville a happy and successful one.
The docking at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port aims to strengthen ties and strengthen good cooperation between the navies of the two countries from 5 to 9 July 2022 (4 days). Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I Council Validation, Khan Meanchey, Deputy District Governor Introduces New Officials to Continue to Serve Citizens
(Phnom Penh): This morning, July 05, 2022, Mr. Dy Rath Khemrun, Deputy Governor of Sangkat Boeung Tumpun 1, 5th mandate of Meanchey district, introduced the validation of Sangkat Councilors and all newly elected members of Sangkat Council. Fifth, pay attention to meet the needs of public services to the people who come to him, such as birth certificates, marriage certificates, death certificates and other services in a timely and transparent manner.
Deputy Governor of Meanchey District further reminded local authorities to strengthen security work in local villages, safe communes, to patrol, ambush or seize crimes such as burglary and to cooperate with local police to eliminate children Gangs and drug problems in the commune.
In addition, Mr. Sous Sarin, who was elected as the Chairman of Boeung Tumpun 1 Sangkat Council of the 5th mandate, was determined to strictly implement the Constitution, laws, regulations and guidelines of the leadership, and strengthen the unity and solidarity. Internal councils, commune officials, village officials and other stakeholders.
In addition, the newly elected Sangkat Councilors promised to promote the implementation of the Village-Sangkat Safety Policy more effectively in order to maintain better security, safety and harmony for the people, and strive to use the budget allocated by the Government and the Treasury. Additional funds from philanthropists in a transparent and efficient manner to contribute to the further development of the local community.
He will promote the provision of public services, both demand and request services, closer to the people to contribute to improving the lives and well-being of the people, strive to strengthen non-judicial dispute resolution mechanisms to gain the trust of the people. Prepare intervention forces for dealing with disasters and other problems that may eventually occur locally.
After the announcement of the first meeting of the new Sangkat Council, Mr. Dy Rath Khemrun, together with the members of the People's Council, teachers, Sangkat officials, continued to eat noodles with the team in a friendly and happy atmosphere under the roof. Peace.
