Commentary: Increasing direct flights between China and Cambodia is a good sign for tourism and the Cambodian economy
(Phnom Penh): Senior officials of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and tourism workers in Cambodia expect that the reopening of direct flights between Cambodia and China will boost the number of tourists and investors coming to Cambodia. After being temporarily reduced due to the global Kovid-19 outbreak.
This positive expectation comes after a commitment between HE Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, and HE Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China in Myanmar. Recently July 3.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodia Travel Agency, told the Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that the agreement between the Cambodian and Chinese diplomats to increase direct flights between the two countries was a good sign for tourism and Cambodia's economic growth.
She said that in the past, Chinese tourists had difficulty traveling to and from each other due to the high cost of air tickets and the difficulty of booking tickets due to the low number of flights between the two countries and the strict conditions for operators. Travel to China.
"Tourists lack the means of transportation, making airfare more expensive and not only more difficult to book," said Chhay Sivlin. "So if we have a little more variety of flights, it will boost the flow of tourists as well as more business travel and can boost economic growth."
His Excellency believes that the Chinese side will increase the number of flights and reduce the shortage of passengers for short-term travelers, which will increase the air transport sector between Cambodia and China, especially passengers. Tourists and investors.
He said: "Investment relations, economy, administration, especially tourists will be improved when we open the reception of air tourists. For those who are already vaccinated. "This increase in flights is a sign of improvement."
According to the forecast of the International Civil Aviation Organization and the International Tourism Organization, by the end of 2024 or the beginning of 2025, the number of air travelers will increase to the same level as in 2019, when there was no Kovid-19 explosion in the world.
