(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of July 05, 2022, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, chaired a meeting to resolve disputes between 136 families and ANVIP Real Estate Co., Ltd. regarding the implementation of the purchase contract. Flat / Hybrid villa for sale located in Ota Sek village, O'Oknha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun agreed to submit a program to resolve construction disputes, termination of the construction contract of Borey VIP Company with the people who are customers and provided an opportunity for the people's representatives and company representatives to make suggestions to resolve.
In this meeting, both parties agreed to respect and abide by the following conditions:
* Second: Borey VIP Company will hand over the title deed and transfer documents to any customer who has paid 100% of the contract within 8 months from August 1, 2022 onwards.
* Third: Both parties agree to the competent authorities to monitor the implementation of the construction work of Borey VIP.
* Fourth: Borey VIP Company must continue the construction from August 1, 2022 and allow the competent authorities to monitor and evaluate the progress of construction during the beginning of September 2022 so that customers continue to pay. To Borey by mutual agreement between Borey VIP Company, customers and provincial administrative team.
* Fifth: For customers who have not paid in full, must continue to pay according to the contract when Borey VIP Construction Company achieves the proportion of the amount paid by the customer (according to the assessment of professional officers).
* Sixth: Borey VIP and the client agree to comply with the above agreement, in case any party does not comply with the above agreement, that party is willing to take responsibility before the law.
He said farmers' pepper exports this year were easier than last year after the 19-Kovid outbreak was eased by Cambodia's main market, Vietnam, which accounts for about 80 percent of Cambodia's pepper exports, as well as exports to Thailand and Europe. . However, the price does not seem to change better than last year, around 13,000 riel per kilogram.
She said that for the pepper market and the price of pepper in Memot area this year is better than last year, with traders coming to collect from the plantation for export. In the Memot area, last year farmers sold pepper for an average of 10,000 riel, but this year they can sell an average of more than 12,000 riel to 13,000 riel and up to 15,000 riel per kilogram at the beginning of the season.
According to a report by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in the first five months of 2022, pepper exports reached more than 5,558 tons, down 25.5 percent. More than 5,131 tons were exported to Vietnam, 355 tons to Germany, 21 tons to Taiwan, 13 tons to Malaysia, 10 tons to France and to Belgium, Japan, the Czech Republic, Canada, the United States, India, the United Kingdom, Kazakhstan, Korea and Australia. .
