(Siem Reap): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, led the celebration of the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health under the theme "Working Together to Build a Culture of Safety and Positive Health" and made some recommendations. To encourage all parties to participate in the implementation of measures to prevent occupational accidents in enterprises and establishments.
The celebration of the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health is an international campaign organized by governments, employers' associations and unions of member countries of the International Labor Organization (ILO) around the world every year to commemorate workers. Employees who have lost their lives due to occupational accidents and occupational diseases in the workplace and to promote decent work, safety and occupational health.
According to the International Labor Organization (ILO) 2022, there are an estimated 3 million deaths worldwide due to occupational accidents and occupational diseases. This number is a reminder to all ILO member countries to continue to work on occupational safety and health.
In response to the theme of the day, Mr. Ith Sam Heng requested all parties to continue to take positive measures to prevent occupational accidents as well as to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the workplace, including increasing dialogue. Society on Occupational Safety and Health in every workplace, considering this issue as a priority right like any other fundamental right.
He proposed to participate in the implementation of the approval of the inclusion of occupational safety and health as a core work to be considered after the addition to the existing Convention 155 and 187. Participate in sharing good practices and experiences of employers and workers from enterprises, companies, establishments to other enterprises.
He proposed to continue to implement the standard operating principles on the operation and management of factories in the new normal course in the context of Kovid-19 disease and to instruct workers to clean their hands regularly in the workplace.
He called for increased attention to disinfection in the workplace, production facilities and shared use areas, and ensured that social gaps were maintained in the workplace and outside as much as possible, and instructed workers to Wear a mask regularly and adhere to the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
