The launch of the KHQR system was attended by Ms. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, Dr. Kong Mary, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chair of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Implementation of the Identification System. Digital customers and many other bank officials.
Ms. Chea Serey said that the official launch of the KHQR system was made to make it easier for customers to pay securely, conveniently and with standard.
Ms. Chea Serey said that the establishment of the KHQR system in conjunction with banking and payment service providers has been competing for the introduction of innovative digital payment services, especially electronic payments and transfers. Such as internet banking, mobile banking, mobile payment services that include QR Code payments.
QR Code payment is a new payment method that has just appeared on the market, but the service has grown rapidly and gained significant popularity, especially young people can adapt to the technology. Recently, because QR Code payments are easy, fast and secure, especially in the context of the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
She said that payments in this way have become an important factor in changing the attitude of the Cambodian people to switch to digital payments instead of cash, and an important part to support business activities to be able to continue to operate normally by cutting. Reduce the impact of Kovid-19 on the Cambodian economy to a certain extent and contribute to economic recovery.
At the same time, the payment according to the QR Code also contributes to the improvement of the financial environment in line with the National Strategy on the Financial Environment 2019-2025 and the orientation towards the Royal Government's digital economic and social policy 2021-2035. .
She added that QR Code payments have greatly supported and facilitated digital payment transactions, but there are still some challenges that need to be addressed and addressed. More from the authorities and stakeholders to ensure sustainable development.
Mr. Sok Choeun, Member of the Board of Directors of the Banking Association of Cambodia and Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, stated that the launch of the KHQR system has made a significant contribution to the development and modernization of the system. Pay in Cambodia to facilitate payments, improve the financial environment and promote innovation in financial technology in the banking and financial sector.
