Please be informed that Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Preah Kosomak, a hospital equipped with modern medical equipment, has been completed and was officially inaugurated on Monday, March 21, 2022. The inauguration ceremony of a new modern hospital in Phnom Penh was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
The Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Preah Kosomak, commonly known as Lok Sang Hospital by Cambodians, was built and equipped at a cost of more than 80 million US dollars with a grant from the Chinese government.
The construction of this hospital was started on October 30, 2018, taking 39 months. The new hospital building is built on a land area of more than 13,000 square meters, with 11 floors and a length of 53 meters. Divided into outpatient, emergency, medical technology, general medicine, obstetrics, gynecology, and other support services. On the roof of the building, there is a helicopter landing pad weighing 3 to 5 tons.
The hospital is equipped with modern medical equipment and has beds for up to 400 patients. The hospital also has a traditional Chinese medicine clinic and is treated by Chinese doctors. Another 231 vehicles were inspected and fined on July 4, 2022
