(Takeo): On the occasion of the meeting to strengthen the implementation of the role of judicial police officers in Daun Keo Municipality on Monday morning, July 4, 2022, Mr. Ek Chheng Huot, Prosecutor of Takeo Provincial Court, instructed the judicial police officers to Perform duties and responsibilities in accordance with the law, especially not to take serious criminal cases out of court.
He said that in resolving extra-judicial cases, judicial police officers could only settle civil cases that were more lenient, while criminal or criminal cases could not be settled out of court.
"I absolutely forbid taking a criminal case or a rape case out of court," he said. "All these cases must be sent to the prosecutor's office for legal action."
Mr. Ek Chheng Huot also instructed the judicial police officers to follow the law on how to record, facts, evidence and detention of minors and to take care to suppress crimes at the local level by reporting to the prosecutor.
