Mr. Chuk Chumnor, Director of the Department of Tourism Product Development and Director of the Secretariat of the CDC, presented the main objectives of the Master Plan: to promote the development of Mondulkiri as an international eco-tourism destination and an important province in Supply flowers, vegetables, fruits and meat to meet domestic demand and reach exports to overseas markets.
Mr. Chuk Chumnor continued that the master plan for tourism development in Mondulkiri province has set the vision of the long-term implementation framework (2021-2035) based on four main visions:
First, Mondulkiri must be identified as an international eco-tourism destination and an important province in the supply of flowers, vegetables, fruits and meat to meet domestic demand and reach exports to foreign markets.
Second, by 2035, the number of international tourists to Mondulkiri will increase to about 900,000, while the number of domestic tourists will increase to about 2 million, creating about 80,000 jobs and generating about 500 direct income. Million dollars and indirectly about 1 billion dollars with a double efficiency coefficient injected into the national economy and the economy of Mondulkiri province.
Third, to contribute to the northeastern region with Mondulkiri as the economic pole; fourth, after Phnom Penh, coastal areas and Siem Reap, and to integrate Mondulkiri with other parts of the country and region.
Fourth, maintain a strong balance between economic development, tourism and cross-sectoral support with the conservation of natural resources, indigenous cultural heritage, ensure the maximum fruits of socio-economic development based on the principle of equitable distribution of benefits. Reach stakeholders.
According to Chuk Chumnor, the master plan identifies key priorities, including:
1: Ecotourism and ecotourism corridors of the five wildlife sanctuaries, which allow only investment and development of environmentally conscious tourism activities.
2: Busra Cultural and Ecotourism Corridor - Dak Dam, which encourages the development of only ecotourism and ecotourism activities connected with indigenous cultures.
3: Sen Monorom city, which is a collection of multi-purpose tourism activities.
4: Oreang district area connected with the development of Mondulkiri airport, which can be developed as a satellite area connected to Sen Monorom city.
5. The urban area of Koh Nhek district, which has the potential to be developed as a tourist center in the future, and the development is more extensive than in the conservation area.
6: Integrated tourist areas along the border, which allow the development of integrated resorts, etc.
He added that the six strategic objectives are divided into 121 implementation activities and 16 priority projects, and 28 relevant ministries and institutions are responsible for implementation.
As for the private sector, Mr. Thong Khon also asked companies and investors to seize the opportunities of Mondulkiri province to raise development projects and investments in both tourism and other related sectors to jointly achieve the set vision. Exit.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also encouraged Mondulkiri to be ready to seize the opportunities for the development of tourism, which is growing significantly based on the strength of its potential. The Royal Government issued a sub-decree on. Organization and Functioning of the Ministry of Justice
