Validation of Pong Teuk Commune Councilors, Romduol District, Deputy Provincial Governor Introduces 13 Points to Perform Their Roles Well and Avoid Discrimination against Citizens
(Svay Rieng): On the occasion of announcing the validity of Pong Teuk commune councilors in Romduol district, Svay Rieng province, on the morning of July 4, 2022, Mr. Ros Pharith, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng province, introduced 13 points for commune chiefs and commune councils to implement. Roles and responsibilities to respond to the needs and interests of all citizens fairly and fairly and not to adhere to political tendencies.
On that occasion, Mr. Ros Pharith warmly praised and congratulated all the members of Pong Teuk Commune Council of the 5th mandate who received the love, satisfaction and support of the people through the election. On Sunday, June 5, 2022, to continue to lead Pong Toek commune for further development in all fields.
The 13 recommendations of the Deputy Governor include:
* First, even though commune councils are elected directly by the people in their commune, they must abide by the constitution, laws and regulations in force.
* Second: After the date of this validation meeting, the first priority of the new mandate Commune Council is to review, prepare and approve its internal regulations, which are the rules and regulations of the meeting and the working mode of the new mandate. Commune / Sangkat Councils and Committees of Commune / Sangkat Councils in accordance with Instruction No. 014 Sanon dated 08 June 2017 of the Ministry of Interior on the preparation of internal regulations of Commune / Sangkat Councils.
* Third: The next task is for the new commune council to meet to review the development projects and service projects remaining from the previous mandate.
* Fourth: Commune councils of the fifth mandate must continue to implement the budget and development projects of commune councils of the previous mandate.
* 5th: Review the composition of the committees or committees of the 4th mandate Commune Council to make adjustments according to the composition and requirements of the 5th mandate Sangkat Council.
* 6: This 5th Mandate Commune Council shall continue to implement the decisions and regulations of the 4th Mandate Sangkat Council that have been decided correctly and effectively in the absence of any new decisions and norms. Instead, no.
* Seventh: Based on the five-year development plan of the fourth mandate commune council, the fifth mandate commune council must prepare its five-year development plan in accordance with the principles and procedures of the defined development planning process.
* Eighth: In addition, commune councils must pay attention to and promote accountability and transparency in the performance of their work on a regular basis.
9th: To cooperate and mobilize all the people in the commune to successfully implement all the policies of the Royal Government, especially to promote the participation in the implementation of the policy of "safe villages, communes, sangkats" of the Royal Government. 7 kinds of property.
10th: The provision of public services in all areas to the people is one of the important roles and responsibilities of the main roles and responsibilities of each commune administration to respond and address requests. And the necessary needs of the people.
* Eleventh: For more than two years, the crisis of epidemic 19 has seriously affected the economy and livelihood of the people in Cambodia.
* Twelfth: Based on the Anti-Corruption Law, all Sangkat Councilors have an obligation to declare their assets and liabilities.
13th: The last point, Mr. Ros Pharith highlighted the important points of the process of free democracy, multi-party elections and social development.
