Through official Facebook, Mr. Prak Sokhon confirmed that this visit, he surveyed the local situation more based on the exchange of views with various actors on the progress and obstacles surrounding the implementation of the five-point consensus.
"Over the past four days, we have focused on providing humanitarian assistance and support to Myanmar in the fight against Kovid-19," he said. These factors will contribute to achieving the core objectives of the "ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Consultation Meeting for Myanmar" in Phnom Penh in early May.
"I also urge all stakeholders to deepen mutual understanding and negotiate more, as this is the most obvious way to return to normalcy and seek peace and stability," he said. Long-term.
Prak Sokhon hopes to better understand the history, culture and people of Myanmar as he travels to the great city of Bakan on July 4 to attend a ministerial meeting. Foreign Affairs of the 7th Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation.
