On the morning of July 2, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, accompanied by Mr. Ek Phan Phanthavong, continued to meet with representatives of seven political parties in Myanmar.
On the afternoon of July 2, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon continued to meet and exchange views with the Ambassador of France, the United States, the European Union and the Chargé d'Affaires of the Australian Embassy in Myanmar.
The talks exchanged views on the progress of the five-point unanimous agreement, including the provision of humanitarian assistance to the people of Myanmar.
After concluding his second working visit to Myanmar, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon will attend the 7th Ministerial Meeting of the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation (MLC) to be held on July 4, 2022. Bagan, Myanmar.
