(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra's Tik Tok social media account has been gaining traction by promoting the names and presence of wildlife in Cambodia's natural resource protection areas.
In order to raise awareness among the Cambodian people about wildlife and rare species in Cambodia, Mr. Neth Pheaktra has prepared a video showing each species recorded by a camera embedded in the forest and describing information related to both species. That. These wildlife videos have received a lot of attention from Tik Tok social media players.
Some videos have been viewed nearly 1 million times, some videos have been viewed more than 300,000 times, 200,000 times and more than 100,000 times. Apart from clicking, these videos are also widely distributed.
Speaking to Fresh News on July 2, 2022, Mr. Net Pheaktra said, "This is a strategy to promote the natural resources of wildlife in Cambodia, especially to provide knowledge about the various species of wildlife that Cambodia has. To cultivate the spirit of people to love more natural resources and participate in the protection and conservation of natural resources and wildlife.
The spokesman confirmed that Cambodia is globally recognized as a country rich in biodiversity of about 5,000 species. Some species are rare animals that people have never known or heard of, but never seen. Therefore, the promotion of all kinds of animals to the people as part of raising awareness of the presence of animals in Cambodia and participate in protection and conservation.
The Secretary of State said: "For the dissemination of the name and presence of wildlife through this social network, it is the mainstreaming of all means of wildlife information in the sense that all citizens have access to information from The presence of animals in Cambodia and join the Ministry of Environment and all relevant ministries and institutions to protect wildlife to survive.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra pointed out that the images that were published were from the installation of automatic cameras by professional officers in the protected areas of Cambodia. The information received from this wildlife shows that Cambodia is proud of its many species, sometimes rare, that the world does not have only Cambodia.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added, "This promotion is also part of cultivating the spirit of love for wildlife and change the attitude of people to participate in preventing and stopping the eating of wild animals and stop trapping and hunting."
The senior official of the Ministry of Environment also thanked the people who used social media to support his Tik Tok social network, saying: "I will try to research and promote the wildlife species that Cambodia has. Sharing knowledge and participating in conservation, and please help to support as much as possible.
