Mine action is not just about clearing mines from land mines. Mine action focuses on the people and society, as well as the possibilities for them to live a dignified and prosperous life.
Currently, nearly one million people across the Kingdom of Cambodia are at risk as they live and work and work in areas with landmines and explosive remnants of war that continue to kill and injure people. And scare the community. These hinder development and rehabilitation and disrupt the livelihoods of people in rural areas.
UNDP is ready to continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Mine Authority. UNDP would like to see significant achievements in mine action, hoping to share these best practices during this time, the celebration of the 30th anniversary of mine action in Cambodia, and at planned global and regional events. For mine action this year.
