On the occasion of the International Day Against Drug Abuse on June 26, 2022, Prince Sar Kheng asserted that the exploitation and use of these substances could be a barrier and a gateway to drug use or Factors leading to drug use.
In connection with this case, the Ministry of Health has issued a statement showing the serious health effects caused by the use of e-cigarettes or Vape that transmit nicotine and e-cigarettes contain different amounts of nicotine. 99% of e-cigarettes contain nicotine.
The Ministry of Health claims that there is evidence that the use of e-cigarettes causes health effects, addiction, serious heart and lung damage and even death. When using e-cigarettes, chemicals and nicotine are absorbed into the body and into the smoker's brain.
E-cigarette use among children and adolescents has a serious impact on brain development, leading to long-term consequences for brain development and possibly impairing memory, learning and anxiety. Feelings. E-cigarette trials are leading the way for young people to become regular smokers and lead to other drug use in the future.
