The Royal Government announces the implementation of the social security system for pensions for individuals under the Labor Law
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced a social security pension system for individuals subject to the provisions of the Labor Law. This is according to the inter-ministerial prakas of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, obtained by Fresh News on July 1, 2022.
On March 4, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued a sub-decree on the social security system for pensions for individuals subject to the provisions of the Labor Law.
This sub-decree aims to introduce a social security system for pensions for individuals subject to the provisions of the Labor Law through defining the mechanisms, conditions, procedures and procedures for registration of contributions, payment of contributions, rates of interest, claims and Provision of Talak.
This sub-decree applies to all persons subject to the provisions of the Labor Law, including persons working in two or more places.
