(Singapore): Forecasts show that from now until mid-July, Singapore will experience hotter and drier weather, with maximum daily temperatures likely to be between 33-34 degrees Celsius for most days. This was released by CNA on Friday, July 1, 2022.
In a statement issued on Friday, the Singapore Meteorological Agency said daily maximum temperatures were expected to reach a maximum of 35 degrees Celsius for several days. At the same time, there may be some hotter nights, about 28 degrees Celsius.
