The Senior Minister brought the Malay-Khmer dictionary, which was officially approved by the Malaysian Institute of Language and Literature in early 2022, by Zakaria Adams after translating the Al-Quran into Khmer before That he passed away. World Bank: Cambodia's economy is growing again but has to cope with the crisis of rising oil prices
In the first half of 2022, exports were valued at 4.8 billion US dollars, up 26 percent from the same period in 2021, the report said. Growing traditional sectors such as garments, travel goods and footwear continue to grow, while new industries such as electronics and auto parts are emerging and exports to the United States are booming. Recover.
Despite the strong economic momentum, the recovery process has been slow due to declining demand in the global market. The relentless rise in fuel and food prices in the world market is driving inflation higher, and in Cambodia, poor and vulnerable households with limited savings are likely to suffer the most. The oil crisis.
The fiscal deficit is expected to widen to 6.3 percent of GDP as the government continues to spend on programs to help the poor. The Cambodian spokesman said that the strategy of "living with Kovid-19" has enabled the economy to recover. But the road ahead is still unclear.
"Rising global oil and food prices due to the war in Ukraine are adding to the hardships of the poor and will slow down poverty," she said. Also. "The government's cash transfer program, which has been very important in helping poor families cope with the epidemic, will need to continue."
In the medium term, the economy is expected to grow at an average of 6 percent per year, thanks to favorable new investment laws accompanied by bilateral trade agreements to boost investment and trade. This report recommends a number of policies that can support economic recovery activities.
Recommendations include the need to continue efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, to further strengthen the trust of consumers and investors, to boost exports, especially agricultural products, through trade facilitation and to reduce costs. Doing business, and continuing to balance retail prices in the market.
These reforms need to take the form of a leading government institutional and agency approach for a comprehensive overview of the development of the logistics sector at the national level and at trade gateways.
