Indonesian president claims handing over Zelensky's message to Putin
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Indonesian President Joko Widodo has said he will hand over a message from Ukrainian President Vladimir Putin to Russian President Vladimir Putin during a visit to Moscow on Thursday. This was released by Reuters on Friday, July 1, 2022.
"I have already handed over Zelensky's message to Putin," Widodo said after meeting with Putin. The Indonesian president added that he was also ready to help start a relationship between Putin and Zelensky, but did not elaborate on Zelensky's message.
Widodo's visit to Moscow comes at a time when Indonesia is under pressure from the West not to invite Putin to the G20 summit in Bali in November. But Jakarta has invited both Zelensky and Putin to the summit.
