This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen released more than 1 million juveniles and fish at Ang Trapeang Thmor to celebrate National Fish Day
(Phnom Penh): On Friday morning, July 1, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, released more than 1 million baby fish and fish in Ang Trapeang Thmor in Poi Char commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province. Samdech Techo's presence at Ang Trapeang Thmor today is the second time, while the first time Samdech Techo inaugurated the pool after repair and renovation in March 2006.
Release of juvenile and juvenile fish today to celebrate the 1st of July Fish Day and to make the pond pond rich in diverse fish species and thriving to other areas can be accessed to other fishing grounds Meet the needs of the people.
According to a report by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, about 1 million young fish and breeds will be released, including catfish, catfish, catfish, catfish and squid. Including endangered species such as carp, turtles and frogs. In addition to releasing juveniles and breeds, the program also plans to release another 200,000 freshwater lobsters.
Please note that Trapeang Thmor Reservoir, where Samdech Techo released the young fish and mackerel, is a large irrigation system and a beautiful tourist resort located in Poi Char commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province. This large reservoir is surrounded by a dam 10 km long from east to west and 7 km long from north to south.
During the rainy season, Trapeang Thmor Reservoir can store about 180 million cubic meters of water. In the dry season, the reservoir can hold 120 million cubic meters of water, which can irrigate 25,000 hectares of wet paddy and 12,000 hectares of dry paddy.
Torture and malnutrition have resulted in the deaths of tens of thousands of Cambodians at the Ang Trapeang Thmor dam site, with tens of thousands of Cambodians dumping their bones at the dam site. Stone pond.
After the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, the geography of Phnom Srok district remained highly favorable for farming, but the people's challenge was the lack of water for irrigation. Seeing this, the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, with financial support from the Government of Japan and the Asian Development Bank (ADB), decided to rehabilitate and improve this stone pond to draw water for irrigation and use.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, led by Minister Lim Kean Hor, began the process of rehabilitating and repairing the reservoir in 2004 and was inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in March 2006.
From 2014 to 2016, the budget of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to repair the 21-kilometer-long Pleung Ang Dam and the 10-kilometer-long embankment will be implemented by the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology. From 2020 to 2021, the government's budget for flood relief in 2020 will repair 10 km of light dams and 15 km of main canals implemented by the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology.
From 2019 to 2021, dig 216 foot canals in the Ang Trapeang Thmor system and construct 33 art structures on foot canals implemented by the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology.
