More than 3,000 people in Banteay Meanchey province were taken to find 19 Kovid before receiving Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the National Fish Day ceremony tomorrow
(Banteay Meanchey): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen will preside over the National Fish Day on July 1, 2022 tomorrow at Trapeang Thmor Reservoir in Trapeang Thmor Kandal Village, Poi Char Commune, Phnom District. Banteay Meanchey District.
In order to receive Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Member of National Assembly and Senate, Provincial Governor, Deputy Provincial Chairman, Provincial Councilors, Provincial Councilors, Provincial Government Officials, Provincial Halls, 3 units, and directors of the Department of Reach, Banteay Meanchey Province, attended the inspection in the morning. June 30, 2022 in the provincial hall.
During the sampling, Mr. Ou Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, stated that the Royal Government decided to establish the National Fish Day through Sub-Decree No. 99 dated September 25, 2002 in order to inspire people to contribute to the protection, conservation and development of the fisheries sector in the direction of guarantee. Sustainability of fishery resources for economic, social and environmental benefits.
He added that on this National Fish Day, the Royal Government has instructed all ministries, state institutions, provincial halls, public enterprises, private enterprises, community associations and educational institutions to inspire government officials, police officers, soldiers, students and people to respect the law and protect resources. Fisheries. Since 2003, Fish Day has been celebrated annually, except in 2020 and 2021, due to the global crisis of 19 communicable diseases.
