The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will visit Ang Trapeang Thmey again on July 1, 2022 to celebrate the National Fish Day and release about one million fish fry. In March 2006, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had already visited Trapeang Thmor Reservoir to inaugurate the reservoir after repair and renovation.
Before the arrival of the reception for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's high presence tomorrow, the national and provincial event organizers worked together to organize the event venue to ensure that the event went as planned. Leave.
Taking time to inspect the venue, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Mr. Oum Rath gave a short interview with Fresh News to recall the history of the construction of the new pool and the benefits of the new pool for the people, especially for Irrigate the rice.
The governor of Banteay Meanchey province said that Ang Trapeang Thmor was originally a normal farmland of the people. Only during the Khmer Rouge regime did the Khmer Rouge leaders force people to dig up land to build dams to hold water for farming in the area.
But the construction was not yet complete, and it failed when the brutal regime was overthrown by the National Salvation Front on January 7, 1979. According to the provincial governor, during the construction of Ang Trapeang Thmor, the Khmer Rouge leaders forced the people to work very hard, work overtime and not eat enough.
The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, led by Minister Lim Kean Hor, began the process of rehabilitating and repairing the reservoir in 2004 and was inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in March 2006.
Currently, Ang Trapeang Thmor can store about 180 million cubic meters of water during the rainy season. In the dry season, the reservoir can hold 120 million cubic meters of water, which can irrigate 25,000 hectares of wet paddy and 12,000 hectares of dry paddy.
Mr. Oum Rath said that after Ang Trapeang Thmor was rehabilitated and improved, many benefits of farming for the people in Phnom Srok and some parts of Preah Net Preah district were passed. He said that the new pool, in addition to providing water for people to farm twice a year, also provides fish and tourist attractions.
The Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province considered this Ang Trapeang Thmor pool as a legacy of the blood and tears of the Khmer Rouge regime and turned it into a place that provided a happy smile for the people in the district to meet peace under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
"This used to be a tragic place, a place of tears during the Democratic Kampuchea regime, where a lot of Cambodians were killed," he said. But now, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, set out a win-win policy that brings peace, makes people strive to grow and sustain their livelihoods.
According to the provincial governor, the provincial authorities also plan to turn the Ang Trapeang Thmor area into a more attractive tourist destination in the future to contribute to improving people's livelihoods by earning more income from farming.
Please note that Ang Trapeang Thmey is located in Poi Char Commune, Phnom Srok District, Banteay Meanchey Province, more than 60 kilometers from the provincial town and more than 400 kilometers from Phnom Penh. You can travel to Ang Trapeang Thmor on National Road 6, drive about 20 km from Kralanh district town, you will see a right turn, which turns into Phnom Srok district town and ride from Pram Hel district town. Another 7 kilometers will reach this pool of rock.
Ministry of Commerce decides to postpone the registration of online businesses until July 3, 2022
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce has issued a notification on the extension of fines for applying for e-business licenses or licenses. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received on June 30, 2022.
Pursuant to Notification No. 0528, dated March 2, 2022, on the Delay of Fines for Delaying the Application for a License or Commercial License. The electronic system will be due on July 1, 2022.
Observing that a large number of sole proprietors and companies came to the Ministry of Commerce to apply for e-commerce licenses or licenses, the Ministry of Commerce decided to extend the fine date until July 3. 2022 at 17:00.
Natural persons, sole proprietorships or companies can come to get the number to apply at the Business Registration Department of the General Department of Business Services or at the Provincial Department of Commerce where natural persons, sole proprietorships or companies are located every working hour from Keep informed.
The Ministry of Commerce would also like to point out that businesses that conduct e-commerce operations without the permission of the Ministry of Commerce will be subject to fines and penalties as provided in the Commercial Law. Electronic system.
