The following is the NEC's press release: Three boys chased two suspects and shocked their phones until they were arrested in Po Sen Chey district.
(Phnom Penh): Two suspects were arrested by Po Sen Chey district police and handed over to Sen Sok district police for questioning and legal action after they snatched the phones from three boys and then tried to ride a motorbike. The boy escaped on a motorcycle, chased and shouted that the thieves surprised the police standing on the road to provide security for the authorities.
According to sources, before the incident, the victim boy rode a white Suzuki Kinetic motorcycle out of a house in O Bek Kam commune to buy food in the southern part of the village. However, when they arrived, they could not find anything to buy, so they rode their motorcycles back home.
He then tried to escape on a motorcycle, but the boy chased after him on a motorcycle and shouted that the thieves had surprised the police, who were standing on the road to provide security for the authorities. At that time, the police helped to intercept immediately and handed over to the Sen Sok district police for questioning and legal action.
