According to an ASEAN press release, 2 million doses of the vaccine will be given to the people of Myanmar, especially in hard-to-reach areas, under the 50:50 mechanism of the joint vaccination framework of the Ministry of Health and its partners. Initiated by Cambodia and approved at the ASEAN Humanitarian Assistance Consultation to Myanmar on 6 May 2022 in Phnom Penh.
The details of the provision and management of the vaccine will be determined later by the ASEAN Coordinating Center for Humanitarian Aid and Disaster Management (AHA Center), the ASEAN Secretariat, the Ministry of Health of Myanmar, the Chinese government and relevant partners. The sole purpose is to "leave no one behind in Myanmar."
At the ceremony, the Deputy Prime Minister also said that "humanitarian aid should not be painted. All stakeholders, including external partners, should set aside political differences and gather under a humanitarian umbrella to gradually improve the situation. "No matter what part of Myanmar, it is all important and the most important thing is to take the first step."
