(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on June 30, 2022, urged and called on all business owners of private security institutions to continue to send their agents to receive training and skills of private security agents. To strengthen the quality of its services to customers to better participate in maintaining security and social order.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khy's call was made during the closing ceremony of the 38th Private Security Agency refresher course organized by the Department of Private Security Management with a total of 137 participants.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi emphasized that private security agencies now play an important role in maintaining security and social order with law enforcement forces, so to ensure this participation is more effective, it requires agents All private security is highly competent as well.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police continued that the trainees who have received this training must share the knowledge they have gained with their colleagues or team and use it in a targeted manner to improve the quality of work in the unit. Make changes to gain the trust and encouragement of business owners or customers.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi advised the private security agencies to see or suspect any illegal activities, especially drug offenses, regardless of where they are standing or where the private security agencies must report immediately. To the local authorities to jointly prevent and suppress crimes in a timely manner.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, said that up to now, 38 private security agency training courses have been conducted, including the Deputy Chief of National Police of the Department of Private Security Management and the Capital Police Commission. A total of 137 participants (08 females) and a total of 6,766 participants (160 females).
The lieutenant general continued that the training course aims to meet the need to increase the capacity to become a qualified and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of security and safety. Order and life of the people as well as improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokha Raksmey also requested all private security agencies to report the situation or crime that occurred in their respective targets to the local authorities or professional authorities to jointly prevent and suppress. Offenses.
