The event was supported by the Demining Project for Results and was attended by Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Representative of Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Chey District, District Administration, Armed Forces, Commune Council, Teachers, Citizens and Students. .
In his welcoming remarks, Mr. Ly Sary spoke about the situation of landmines and explosive remnants of war in Banteay Meanchey province, which was affected by the protracted war in Cambodia, which caused many deaths, disabilities and injuries, in particular. It also creates obstacles to local development activities.
Mr. Ly Sary continued that the activities that caused the mine danger are due to the risk of encroachment on new lands that we have not yet cleared and the encroachment on non-timber forest products in suspected mine areas that we should consider together. Thoroughly and find preventive measures.
Before concluding, the Senior Minister made five recommendations to students of the same age who are making decisions and planning for the future:
* Get rid of bad habits and waste of time * Be tolerant of yourself and others * Increase self-confidence by making the right decisions * Be able to provide loving service Compassion and compassion for the family, community and society * must choose and prepare the attitude to be happy.
Ministry of Commerce raises awareness of exporters to take more advantage of RECP
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, on the morning of June 29, 2022, presided over the opening of the first series of national seminars on "Understanding the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement". "(Asip) and the procedure for applying for a certificate of origin through the automation system."
The workshop was attended by senior officials from the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, officials from the Ministry of Commerce, representatives of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Cambodian Garment Manufacturers Association, the Cambodian Rice Federation, the Cambodian Footwear Association and other relevant private sector representatives, totaling about 350 people. Figure.
Minister Pan Sosak emphasized that this first national series of workshops is an up-to-date intervention in addition to the outreach mechanisms that the Ministry of Commerce has put in place in the past.
The purpose of this workshop is to spread awareness and information to the private sector, businesses, producers and exporters to seize the opportunities and maximize the benefits of opening markets under the ASEAN Agreement after entry into force. On January 1, 2022 ago.
Minister Pan Sosak stated that the rules of origin under the ASEAN Agreement, which are simple and easy to implement, will help push Cambodia to integrate itself into the regional production chain faster and promote regional economic integration.
Minister Pan Sosak encouraged participants, especially exporters, to make the most of today's workshop by asking the technical staff in charge of technical issues and procedures for applying for a Certificate of Origin. ASP form according to the automation system.
At the same time, the Ministry of Commerce will continue to organize such workshops in each priority area in the provinces - cities with high potential to export products under the framework of the ASEAN Agreement and other free trade agreements. Also.
