"These claims about failure to repay this debt are completely false," he said. He added that Russia had already paid its debts in May.
The 30-day grace period for $ 100 million in interest payments expired on Sunday night, most of which was paid in foreign currency.
Russia has tried to make the payment, but the Russian Ministry of Finance said on Monday that the money had not been transferred to creditors. Receive full payment in advance "but the money is not transferred to the final recipient due to" third party measures ".
"The activities of foreign financial intermediaries are beyond the control of the Russian Ministry of Finance," the statement said.
