(Phnom Penh): The National Consultative Workshop on Economic Diplomacy in the New Orbit, held on June 27, 2022, ended successfully as the seminar requested diplomats to help 5 points . This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, obtained by Fresh News today.
Five points that the whole workshop suggested to diplomats to help include:
1: Disseminate information on the new investment law and potential of Cambodia 2: Further research on the needs of foreign markets and organize business forums with foreign partners 3: Strengthen the sharing of information between ministries - institutions and the private sector 4: Promote dissemination widely From the potential of tourism in Cambodia to enhance the national prestige, as well as 5: Create a team to promote Khmer cuisine on the international stage.
Please be informed that the National Consultative Workshop on Economic Diplomacy in the New Normal Path, organized by the Economic Diplomatic Coordination Team of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs under the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation Special Fund Project at the Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel Closed under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs.
A press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs added that the workshop was initiated for the purpose of:
1: Disseminate the economic diplomacy strategy 2021-2023 more broadly 2: Collect input from relevant ministries and institutions to strengthen inter-ministerial cooperation and with the private sector in economic diplomacy 3: Understand the challenges and shortcomings of implementation Economic diplomacy strategy; and 4: Identify mechanisms to strengthen the capacity and understanding of diplomats and officials involved.
The workshop focused on the role of diplomats in three major sectors, including investment and trade, tourism and Khmer culture and cuisine, with speakers from relevant ministries, institutions and private companies consulting. Opportunities, challenges and mechanisms to maximize the benefits for our people.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon praised the current national consultation workshop and praised the efforts of the Economic Diplomatic Coordination Team, which have achieved major achievements in the past, including:
As the Chairman of the Economic Diplomatic Coordination Working Group, Dr. Nhim Khemara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, also highlighted the importance of the partnership between the relevant ministries and institutions with the private sector in implementing the economic diplomacy strategy and encouraged this cooperation to be even greater. Effective to contribute to the promotion of socio-economic development.
