(Kratie): Ms. Kham Sopheap, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, on June 28, 2022, held a workshop to disseminate the Koh Sam Sip Ecotourism Development Plan 2022-2026 at Kratie University.
Koh Samsip is a wonderful ecotourism community covering three villages: Khsach Leav, Koh Khnhe and Ngon, Chea Chea village, Prek Krieng commune, Sambo district, Kratie province. Spread along the Mekong River, this community is more than 90 kilometers from Kratie provincial town.
Ms. Kham Sopheap highly appreciated all the efforts made by the Kratie Provincial Department of Tourism and its partner organizations to initiate the development plan for the Koh Sam Thip ecotourism community in a realistic, clear, geographical, cultural and traditional manner. The daily life of the people in the area.
