The cocoa grower stated that for the first year, it was not very productive, with only 5 kg or more per plant, but it started to bear a lot of fruit in the following years. There is fruit until the farmers take good care of it and have enough water. It is a weather resistant crop.
Another farmer, Mr. Yoeum Yoeun, who lives in Preah Dak village, Preah Dak commune, Banteay Srei district, mentioned about the above farmers. He stated that cocoa is a regular crop for farmers, that is, they can be harvested weekly when the cocoa is ripe. "This crop can boost the family economy and the economy in the country, especially without migration can turn to study this cocoa crop," Yoeun said.
This farmer told other farmers, if they want to plant, they have to take care of it, especially the water system, if possible, the water system should be better.
