Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department cooperates with Poipet Municipality to organize dengue fever campaign
(Banteay Meanchey): On June 28, 2022, the Department of Health cooperated with the Poipet City Administration with the participation of local authorities in the five communes, the Armed Forces, government officials, teachers, nephews, students, and students. The Red Cross and about 200 health officials have organized a campaign against dengue fever.
Dr. Le Chansangvat said that for Banteay Meanchey province, 40 cases were found but were treated by doctors from the provincial referral hospital. He said that due to the rainy season, which caused the transmission of mosquitoes, tiger bites cause dengue fever, which mostly affects children, so the launch of the campaign today is to promote and send a message to remind people to be interested. And participate in the fight against dengue fever.
According to the doctor, if there is a suspicion of dengue fever, please consult and treat at the health center or hospital near your home quickly and on time, do not treat yourself at home, which can cause serious and difficult to treat. When sent to the hospital.
