Russia vows to retaliate against Japan over Tokyo sanctions on Ukraine over Ukraine aggression
Russia has vowed to retaliate against Japan over its Tokyo sanctions on Moscow over its aggression against Ukraine. This is according to the release by AFP on Monday, June 27, 2022.
Japan has joined the West in attacking Russia with an unprecedented package of sanctions in the four months since Russia began its war against Ukraine.
Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida has said at a summit of the Group of Seven (G7) economies in Germany that Tokyo will impose additional sanctions on 70 Russians. Expanding the embargo on exports to Russia in response to Putin's war in Ukraine.
So far, the Japanese government has already launched a series of sanctions against Russia in response to Russia's war in Ukraine, which the West considers invading, including Belarusian Russians. More than 700 companies, as well as more than 200 Russian and Belarusian companies.
France wants France and Iran, which are under sanctions, to return to the oil market to ease Russia's pressure on energy supplies, which have pushed up prices, French presidential officials say. This is according to the release by Reuters on Monday, June 27, 2022.
France also wants the planned mechanism to reduce oil prices as comprehensive as possible and not be limited to Russian output.
