(Phnom Penh): As an encouragement to journalists who have worked hard in the past and have done well, the Association for Professional Development of Journalists of Cambodia organized a solidarity dinner for journalists and presented the Best Journalist Award. 2022, which was held on the morning of June 27, 2022 at The Grand Palace, Toul Kork, under the presidency of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information.
For the occasion of the Solidarity Dinner, 394 journalists from 42 units and more than 100 guests were invited.
On that occasion, Mr. Hor Kunthea, Representative of the Association of Professional Development of Journalists of Cambodia, stated his position to find ways to establish training courses, seminars, forums frequently and to find Cambodian and foreign trainers with high experience in the field of information to teach you. The press will also try to communicate with overseas partners to provide opportunities to send outstanding journalists to study abroad.
This is a contribution to strengthen the capacity of professional ethics in the field of Cambodian media under the talented leadership of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, and especially the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister. Of Cambodia.
He said that a newspaper that can run for a long time needs to have a lot of information so that viewers know more. Journalists are also good at daring to swim, which means they can write information that they do not understand. Therefore, the professional training of journalists is very important to enable us to survive in the evolving state of technology and the evolution of society.
At the same time, it must be remembered that morality is a coat of arms for journalists, and the Ministry of Information has strived to promote a better professional ethics, because information makes society better, more harmonious and prosperous. For a democratic society, information is very important because in a modern democracy, there must be the participation of the people, depending on having enough information, and the informant is the journalist.
On this occasion, Minister Khieu Kanharith presented awards to journalists who received the 2022 Outstanding Journalist Award for Ethics and Professionalism, a total of 42 people and 45 letters of commendation.
