Mr. Kim Hour, the owner of Green Farm Farm Village, stated that in addition to cultivating the above-mentioned crops, his farm is also preparing to establish a natural tourism area on several hectares of land in Lor Village, Tuol Khpos Commune, Teuk Phos District, which currently grows fruit. 100 hectares of gourds, 5,000 durians, 100 hectares of gourds, and is preparing to build a resort to grow all kinds of fruits, turning the farm into a tourist tourism area for visitors as well.
At the seed farm, he is also digging canals in the farm to irrigate the crops and to raise lobsters and fish to earn extra income and to support the livelihood of the workers working on the farm.
He said that in our plan for the next two or three years, he will set up a factory to collect crops for resale to be packaged for sale in the market under the brand name of Vision Farm in Phnom Penh.
