Ministry to start imposing fines on unregistered online businesses next month
(Phnom Penh): If nothing changes, the Ministry of Commerce will start imposing fines on e-commerce businesses that do not register their businesses from July 1, 2022 onwards.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of June 27, 2022, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that online businesses without permission from the Ministry of Commerce will be accepted. There are fines and penalties as stated in the e-commerce law.
Mr. Pen Sovichet stated, "If the deadline is reached and we still do not apply for a business license, it may result in us being fined by the Ministry of Commerce in accordance with other laws and regulations."
In addition, the senior official of the Ministry of Commerce claimed that the Ministry of Commerce has close cooperation with the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, which is the relevant ministry to monitor the activities of sales or use the Internet to Doing business.
According to Mr. Pen Sovicheat, so far, the Ministry has received more than 300 applications and has registered some, both registration and licensing, but there are still some applications that have not been answered. Due to the lack of some documents to guide the supplement.
At the same time, Mr. Pen Sovichet said that for the past practice, people who are doing business online, as individuals, as legal entities, have a lot of understanding and a series of requests that show the spirit of Understand the obligations that must be met to meet the requirements of the regulatory requirements set by the Ministry or the Royal Government.
Please note that six types of online businesses are exempt from registration, which includes:
First, if you only advertise your goods or services that do not form a contract request, then you are simply advertising as if you had a good agricultural product, but you did not declare the price of your product without creating it. Such contract requests are exempt because you do not provide trading services (but make sure you do not provide trading services).
Second, the reservation of the non-deposit service can provide various information for your customers or users means that there is a chat with you, but there is no deposit service as a whole is not created No contract request, so no registration required.
Fifth, the sale of goods as works of art, for example, as a painter, and they put the painting on their own Facebook to show that they painted or as a sculptor does not require them to apply for a permit. Because it is its pure work.
Sixth: Private online student training or workshop training, etc. The Ministry does not require registration.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated that individuals or business people who are not sure about the registration can go to the Ministry of Commerce for questioning, because the Ministry does not accept all registrations, the Ministry will provide information to business people to know that Obliged to register or obliged to register or subject to exemption.
The business registration service for online businesses at the Ministry of Commerce costs only 200,000 riel for public services and 400,000 riel for legal entities with a validity of two years.
