Tehran has launched the Zuljanah space rocket, sparking outrage in Washington amid speculation over talks, Iranian state television said on Sunday. The 2015 Iran nuclear deal will resume soon. This was released by Reuters on Monday, June 27, 2022.
This is the second time that Tehran has tested the Zuljanah space rocket after the first test in 2021, Iranian state television quoted Iranian officials as saying. However, Iranian state television did not say when, where or when the second test took place. The White House has called the test an act of regional instability.
According to Iranian officials, Zuljanah is a rocket 25.5 meters long and capable of carrying a satellite weighing 220 kilograms that can collect data in low orbit. Iran has often called its tests "research" but the United States has accused Iran's rocket tests of developing intercontinental ballistic missile technology.
