KOICA and Sunjunyang Medical University Center Organize the 2nd Cambodia-Korea Joint Seminar on Ear, Nose and Throat Disease
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and the Sun Joonyang Medical University Center of the Republic of Korea held the 2nd Cambodia-Korea Joint Seminar on Otolaryngology with the Ministry of Health and Hospitals. Preah Ang Duong on June 25, 2022 at the Hyatt Regency Hotel in Phnom Penh.
Relevant units and distinguished guests, including representatives of the Ministry of Health, as well as officials from the Prosecutor's Office, Ang Duong Hospital and Sunjunyang Medical University Center, with a total of more than 120 participants, including seven Korean doctors and five Korean nurses. People attended the workshop.
Mr. Kim Kwang Wook affirmed that the purpose of this second conference is to share and exchange experiences with each other and the skills of each country (Cambodia, Korea) in the field of ear, nose and throat, especially in strengthening Efficacy of joint treatment between the ear, nose, throat, head and neck using a multidisciplinary approach.
Speaking on the occasion, Prof. Dr. Mam Bunheng expressed his deep gratitude to the Government of the Republic of Korea for providing the new building and technical assistance for ear, nose and throat disease at Ang Duong Hospital through the Korea International Cooperation Agency. KOICA) and Sun Joon-young Medical University Center of the Republic of Korea.
During the workshop, the Korean side explained: First: Head and neck surgery, Second: Major cases at Sunjunyang Medical University related to ear, nose and throat, Third: Ear, nose and throat study Throat and Rhinoplasty (Head and Neck) and Fourth: Discussion of the latest surgical techniques related to ear, nose and throat.
The Cambodian side made a presentation on the first: sharing knowledge about the ears, nose, throat, head and neck, the second: sharing knowledge on cosmetic surgery, third: important cases in the ear at Preah Hospital Ang Duong and 4: Major cases in the head and neck at Ang Duong Hospital.
The Government of the Republic of Korea, through the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA-KOICA), has provided a grant of US $ 8 million for the "Capacity Building Project for the Ear, Nose and Throat (ENT) Center in Preah Ang Duong Hospital ”which was implemented from 2018 to 2022.
