India sends relief team to Afghanistan quake victims
New Delhi: India will send emergency relief and technical teams to help the people of eastern Afghanistan after a devastating earthquake that state media reported killed 1,000 people. This is according to the release by the AP on Friday, June 24, 2022.
A ministry statement on Friday said 27 tonnes of relief supplies on the two flights included basic necessities such as family tents, blankets, pillows and sleeping mats.
"The dispatch will be handed over to the United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs and the Afghan Red Crescent Society in Kabul," the statement said.
A magnitude 6.1 earthquake shook the region of Afghanistan about 160 km southeast of Kabul and near the border with Pakistan at dawn on Wednesday (local time). It has killed at least 1,000 people and injured more than 1,500.
