The German parliament has voted to repeal the law, meaning doctors are allowed to provide more information about abortion without fear of reprisals. Technically, abortion is completely illegal in Germany. However, it is allowed under certain circumstances and the procedure must be performed within 12 weeks of pregnancy.
"For almost a century, doctors have been banned and punished by fines for providing specific information," German Justice Minister Marco Buschmann said in a statement. "About methods and possible risks for women who are considering abortion."
The German government launched a plan to repeal the law under a coalition government agreement signed in November.
