Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Restricts Forestry Administration to Establish Strict Patrol Force to Protect Antenna Forest
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, restricted the Provincial Forestry Administration to organize a very strict patrol force to protect the antenna forest, which was transferred from the Ministry of Environment to the Ministry of Agriculture.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak led a team and professional officers to inspect the condition of the antenna forest in Boeung Lvea and Kraya communes, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, June 24, 2022.
After the inspection, it was found that some unscrupulous people had cut down the forest to take ownership of the land, and he urged the professional officers to make the land, confiscate the encroached land and target those who encroached on the forest land to be punished. Follow legal procedures.
He added that the authorities must find the perpetrators of these crimes and to withdraw immediately. He will follow up on this matter on a regular basis, if any involvement is found, he will be punished according to the law.
In Kampong Tralach Commune, Kampong Cham Province, the Cambodian People's Party won 5 seats, the Chairman of the Commune Assistance Team and the Working Group met with party members and people to thank them.
(Kampong Cham): On Friday, June 24, 2022, Oknha Low Heung, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Deputy Chairman of the National Task Force for Tong Tralach Commune, met with newly elected Commune / Sangkat Councilors and Active youth group of the Cambodian People's Party, Tong Tralach commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Chas Choeun, Chief of Tong Tralach Commune, expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the people in Tong Tralach Commune who continue to support the Cambodian People's Party, including participating in many elections, leading to a satisfactory result by receiving Won 5 seats out of 5 (win).
Members of the Candlelight Party, who would like to join the CPP, expressed their gratitude to the CPP through Duke Low Heung and his team for building many achievements, such as roads, schools, libraries, and pagodas. Water wells, commune halls, party departments, police stations, generators and Red Cross branches in Srey Santhor district.
Duke Low Hung added that through the inscription, the slogan that will be with the Cambodian people and leaders of all generations is "Thank you for peace". On the other hand, remembering and thinking about peace every minute will make our country more secure, stable and lasting peace, which is the desire of every Cambodian citizen to have peace and have everything until today.
