(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has announced the procedures and conditions for obtaining a mortgage certificate from the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation, an additional mechanism to support the co-financing project to restore and promote tourism, which was implemented by the Royal Government yesterday. May 17, 2022 ago.
This promotion program was chaired by Mr. Song Tonghap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the Sub-Working Group on Support for Industry and Labor in the Tourism Sector, on behalf of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism on June 24, 2022.
Mr. Song Tonghap said that this additional mechanism will help to solve the problem of seeking collateral for loans in the co-financing project to restore and promote tourism growth.
He added that the loan guarantee program will facilitate tourism businesses that need credit from participating financial institutions and have a shortage of collateral, in which tourism business owners can apply for loans from participating financial institutions in the maximum amount up to $ 400,000 at an annual concessional interest rate of 6.5%, with or without collateral to secure the loan.
Mr. Nolida, Deputy Director General of the Credit Guarantee Corporation of Cambodia, stated that the tourism business must meet a number of qualifications, such as: 1) Business with Cambodian shareholders (holding more than 50% of the shares), 2) Businesses registered with Relevant or unregistered authorities must register after obtaining a credit guarantee and 3) a repayable business.
He stated that in order to obtain a Letter of Guarantee (LG), the tourism business can contact the participating financial institutions to apply for a loan in the co-financing project to restore and promote tourism growth by simply stating that the business needs to apply for a letter. Guaranteed credit? Under the loan approval, the participating financial institution will apply to the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation to provide a letter of guarantee.
As of May 31, 2022, there were 1,196 tourism businesses nationwide that were closed / suspended, of which 498 tourism businesses were closed and 698 places were temporarily closed, resulting in the loss of direct employment. In the tourism sector, a total of 21,998 people.
Mr. Song Tonghap said that the Royal Government's co-financing project combined with the credit guarantee program will be an important financial tool to encourage tourism industry to recover quickly in line with the expectations of the Ministry of Tourism. It will receive 7 million international tourists by 2025 and 11 million domestic tourists by 2023.
The confirmation of the head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps was made in an interview on Cambodia-Vietnam diplomatic relations on June 24, on the occasion of the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, Cambodia-Vietnam (June 24, 1967 - June 24). 2022) and the year of Cambodia-Vietnam friendship 2022.
Regarding the border issue, the Deputy Prime Minister stated: "The remaining 16% of the border that has not been demarcated and demarcated is still a priority for both our countries. In particular, we need to accelerate the work of the border and set up border posts by 6%, which was agreed upon by both leaders to achieve success in the near future.
It should be noted that in terms of demarcation work and border demarcation with Vietnam, Cambodia has achieved 84% of the work progress and is working to negotiate to push for the completion of this work as soon as possible.
At present, Cambodia has a total of 43 border crossings with Vietnam, including 4 seaports, 14 international border gates, 13 bilateral border gates and 12 regional gates. Recently, at the inauguration of infrastructure in the military history area of Techo Koh Thmor X16, the Prime Minister announced that a new Cambodia-Vietnam international gate will be established in this area.
The Deputy Prime Minister also stated that the construction of Cambodia's border with neighboring countries to become a border of peace, friendship, cooperation and development is the vision and strong commitment of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon Unveils Significant Achievements in 55 Years of Cambodia-Vietnam Diplomatic Relations
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, outlined some important achievements in the 55 years of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Vietnam.
In an interview on Cambodia-Vietnam diplomatic relations on the occasion of the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries today, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon highlighted the outstanding achievements in the fields of economy, education, security and Defense, border sector, health sector and cooperation in the following regional and international forums:
* Education The two countries have been exchanging scholarship students regularly since 1981. Vietnam has given us 120 places a year and we have given back 35 places to Vietnam. Cambodia sent 3,967 scholarship students to study in Vietnam from technical secondary to doctoral level between 1981-2021 and 477 Vietnamese students and officials came to study in Cambodia from 2000-2021.
* Security and Defense Forces The two countries' forces, both police and military, have been cooperating to take strong and effective measures to prevent all kinds of criminal activities along the border, such as terrorism, drug trafficking and trafficking. People, smuggling of goods, illegal logging and transnational crime, etc.
Health Sector In the face of the challenges of the Kovid-19 epidemic, the two countries have supported each other in the fight against Kovid-19 in terms of finance, medical equipment and a spirit of solidarity in addition to cooperation. Manage infectious diseases and other diseases through the exchange of information, experience and excellence, especially between border provinces.
DC-Cam's Cham Silk Project was created to preserve the memory of the Cham people about silk and weaving.
(Kampong Cham): The Documentation Center of Cambodia's Cham Silk Project was established to preserve the Cham people's memory of silk and weaving after the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, to raise awareness and disseminate and to plan for future development. . The project will support women and community members to create small-scale handicrafts, starting with a simple idea and a silk skirt.
From 13 to 15 June 2022, a team from the Documentation Center of Cambodia, including Seang Chenda, Long Oun, and Min Sanas, interviewed Cham survivors of the Khmer Rouge regime about their lives. The Khmer Rouge regime and family livelihood with silk weaving, the art of weaving lanterns, design and the use of color in weaving.
Mat Mai Sma, a 72-year-old female resident of Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province, described: “Cham silk weaving allowed me to raise my mother, children and nephews after the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime in 1979. "After the Khmer Rouge regime, my family survived only women and children, so my mother and I worked hard to find fish to sell, save money, buy sports, weave cloth for personal use and provide for the family."
She understood that Cham silk skirts, lanterns, Cham skirts may be lost in the future, because today the Cham girls in the village do not seem to be interested in weaving, which is our tradition. Three Families in Po Rieng District Ask Prey Veng Provincial Authorities for Additional Intervention in Fence Blocking
(Prey Veng): Three families living in Anlong Trea village, Prek Chrey commune, Po Rieng district, Prey Veng province, have requested the Prey Veng provincial authorities and relevant officials to intervene in the case of stone fences blocking their roads, despite the district administration. Prohibit.
Then, on February 28, 2022, Ren Keo Lai led his party to build a stone fence on the road, blocking the entrance to their house without any decision while building the district administration. Po Rieng also temporarily banned the construction of Ren Keo Lay's stone fence, but he continued to do so without fear of the power of the district administration.
However, the three families urged the provincial administration and relevant officials to help find a solution for them, while his house and land have been living and enjoying for a long time and then lost their way. Kovid-19 Techo Santepheap Medical Center completed 30% of construction
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, accompanied by Dr. Yuk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, together with Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, on June 24, 2022, led a technical working group between the Ministry of Health and the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration. Meet with the construction company to check the progress of the construction of Kovid-19 Techo Santepheap Medical Center.
The treatment center is located in Sangkat Kork Rokar, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh, built on an area of nearly 8 hectares with a total of 11,000 beds.
The construction company presented the progress of the construction, confirming that the project has completed more than 30% of the construction, the treatment center has a total of 9 buildings, including 7 treatment buildings, 1 administrative building, 1 staff building.
Dr. Yok Sambath requested the construction company to speed up the construction to complete the construction of 5 buildings by the end of February 2023, while the remaining 4 buildings will be completed in June this year. 2023.
This treatment center will be a new achievement in the Kingdom of Cambodia, Kovid-19 treatment center will be equipped with modern medical equipment in accordance with the standard.
