Economists at the Royal Academy of Cambodia expect the Chinese-led BRICS summit to be a regime change, not based on Western models.
(Phnom Penh): Economic analysts at the Royal Academy of Cambodia expect that the Chinese-led BRICS summit in 2022 will be an economic cooperation that is not based on the Western model, that is, reduce barriers. Protecting the trade of Western countries, such as the United States, is causing problems for the world, especially the production market that comes from China.
Dr. Ky Sereywat, President of the Institute of Chinese Studies of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and an economic analyst, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio on the afternoon of June 23, 2022 that the trade barriers that occurred during the reign of former President Tram last year. 2019 has had a devastating effect on enterprises around the world, and it has also had an impact on US inflation.
He added that according to the new model of trade between the BRICS countries, which include Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa, all of these countries are new industrialized countries, so the world needs goods from all these countries. Necessary. This cooperation is the seed of value-added production chains of each country.
