The National Assembly presents the results of hosting the 5th Annual Meeting of the IPA Advisory Council on Drugs
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Ty Sokun, Secretary of the Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information Committee of the National Assembly, and Mr. Chhay Vanna, Secretary of the Senate Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information Commission, as the Chairman of the Parliamentary Delegation of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
At the opening ceremony of the 5th Annual Meeting of the IPA Advisory Council on Drugs, IPO Secretary General Nguyen Tong Van delivered a welcome address to the meeting, highlighting the challenges and consequences. From drugs in the region and asked the IPA delegates invited to today's meeting to share good experiences in contributing to the fight against drugs to the ASEAN drug-free community.
The 5th Annual Meeting of the IPA Advisory Council on Drugs was followed by a presentation on the sharing of drug experiences by representatives of the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime, ASEAN Senior Officials on Drugs. Addiction and the National Authority for Combating Drugs, citing regional and global challenges to the meeting.
After listening to the above presentation, the meeting continued to have a lively discussion on the draft decision. As a result, the IPA delegation agreed on the content of the draft resolution on "Joint Resolution for a Drug-Free ASEAN" attached to the minutes of the 5th Annual Meeting and signed by the heads of parliament of the seven countries. To submit to the 43rd IPA General Assembly for approval.
