(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, has introduced an urgent measure to crack down on any sand dredging business that violates the law.
The introduction of measures to crack down on the illegal sand dredging business took place on the afternoon of June 23, 2022 at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall after Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Mr. Un Chanda chaired a meeting to discuss this issue with the District Governor. And 35 commune chiefs along the Mekong River.
The provincial governor said that in the past, there was information related to the illegal sand dredging business in some localities, which the Ministry of Mines and Energy allowed them to do sand dredging business by the business owners who did not dredge the sand at the location. According to the Ministry, the pumping of sand with good sand is required according to the market and has caused the loss of many royalties, causing the government to lose revenue for the national budget.
In relation to the above reasons, the Provincial Governor decided to set up urgent measures to organize the means and law enforcement forces to carry out the work of cracking down and strengthening all meat business activities along the Mekong River in Kampong Cham Province, requiring business owners Dredging to the location designated by the Ministry of Mines and Energy in the permit will lead to the elimination of anarchy.
The director of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Mines and Energy, Mr. Ly Chanthy, said that there are 22 licensed companies in Kampong Cham.
Mr. Ly Chanthy said that in the past, the challenge was that the owners of the enterprises had already registered their licenses before doing business, but could not maintain them due to the frequent cuts by fishermen. On the other hand, officials lack the means to crack down when crimes occur.
