Jurin said the free trade agreement (FTA) with Efta would cover not only trade in goods but also trade in services, investment, trade facilitation and environmental issues, and reduce tariffs. Export and import bilaterally.
According to the Bangkok Post, major exports include gems and jewelry, watches and accessories, car watches and accessories, travel accessories, machinery and mechanics, air conditioners and accessories, cosmetics, soaps and skin care products and canned seafood. And processing. Major imports include jewelry, gems, silver, gold, watches and accessories, meat, medicine and medical products.
Thailand has 14 free trade agreements with 18 countries, including the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, which entered into force earlier this year. FTA negotiations with Etta were initiated from 2005 to 2006 but were later suspended.
