The provincial governor said that some time ago, there were comments from teachers in remote rural areas asking the authorities to help solve the problem of local money and special hours, especially contract teachers. At the same time, the settlement of regional money issues has been resolved and yet the hourly wage has not been resolved.
"As for the hourly salary for teachers, it can be opened in August 2022," he said. "But to encourage our teachers, let the relevant departments and units help speed up the work so that teachers can get paid by the end of July 2022."
On that occasion, in order to make the education sector more high quality and efficient, Mr. Un Chanda had the following suggestions:
* First: To further improve the quality of education in all villages, especially the implementation of child-friendly school programs to train the next generation of young people with the ability to grow in all areas: knowledge, skills, technical skills. Virtue, morality and well-being are necessary conditions for real life in our society.
* Second: To further strengthen and expand the amount of education by focusing on collecting school-age children, especially girls, disadvantaged children and minority children and children with disabilities to have the opportunity and good luck. Equally, everyone is enrolled in primary and secondary education in order to achieve the 9-year obligation of basic education, especially in kindergarten.
* Third: To expand the child-friendly schools that are gaining popularity on the international stage to all school districts throughout the province.
* Fourth: Continue to improve the capacity of teachers, strengthen management, monitoring and evaluation in connection with the training of human resources for the rotation and deployment of teachers to places where there is a shortage of teachers appropriately.
* 5th: Continue to maintain, improve and renovate the existing school building, existing facilities and new construction, especially the preparation of the school environment, classrooms to be a friendly place for students.
* Sixth: For program budget, please use this budget in the direction of transparency, accountability and avoid inactivity.
* Seventh: Further strengthen and expand international relations to mobilize resources to help develop the education sector to grow to another level.
* 8th: Please, all principals, parents, guardians must strive to educate and guide their students and children to respect school discipline, family discipline and the law of our society to be consistent, not to wander, to avoid school and home. To commit immoral acts and so on.
Mobile payments boost digital economy development and contribute to China's rural development
(Beijing): In line with the evolution of the era, trading and payments have also evolved from the "takeaway" to cash payments, bank cards and most recently mobile devices, especially mobile phones.
People's purchasing power is an important factor that reflects the living standards of the people. If people do not have access to it, the market will be weak and the national economy will be weak.
Therefore, promoting the purchasing power of the people is an important element of the national economic stimulus policy. However, in the case of China, which has a population of 1.4 billion, if the purchasing power of the people is strong, the Chinese market will be optimistic, but on the contrary, if the purchasing power is weak, the huge market will be like a gourd. Big but big but hollow inside.
In fact, China has grasped its market share excellence by striving to boost and increase consumer consumption by day, and payment methods are becoming more convenient day by day.
But for the elderly who are not very computer literate, online payment has not brought much convenience to them, so the Chinese banking group and major Chinese digital technology companies have teamed up to develop online payment software. A special mobile device is a mobile phone that provides easy payment for people of all ages.
The era is constantly evolving, the development of each country also has to adapt to the current of the era, the competitive power of the traditional economy has gradually weakened, prompting countries around the world to focus on the development of digital economy. A new option of national economic development in this era.
According to statistics, there are currently nearly 900 million mobile payment users in China, with more than 400 trillion yuan a year, contributing significantly to the development of the digital economy.
Promoting marketable agricultural products to increase farmers' incomes is part of China's policy to strengthen poverty alleviation, which allows farmers to grow crops without having to worry about a lack of markets, which has contributed to the recovery. Rural development, in which mobile payments have played an important role in connecting the product trade between urban and rural areas.
On the other hand, people living in remote rural areas can also buy modern equipment online with fast home delivery that facilitates their lives without having to travel long distances to buy and deliver goods. Myself.
According to statistics, there are now nearly 900 million mobile payment users in China, with more than 400 trillion yuan a year, contributing significantly to the development of the digital economy.
