Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital has strong public support
(Koh Kong): Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital is currently receiving strong support from the public and people in the health sector to treat patients and infrastructure for aesthetics in the hospital premises.
On June 23, 2022, Dr. Chase Chedi, Director of Pediatrics, said that according to the situation of daily pediatric treatment for children for the past six months, the number of children coming for treatment has increased. About 6% higher than in previous years, and the most common diseases in children are respiratory infections and dengue fever.
"Children with respiratory infections are more likely to be affected by climate change, hot weather, rain, dehydration and poor health," she said. Dengue fever is caused by a female mosquito that bites a child, causing dengue fever. Dengue fever is caused by the environment around the house, the environment is not clean, there are pools of water as a habitat for mosquitoes to reproduce.
"In order to avoid dengue fever, you need to take measures to clean up the environment around the villagers, make their homes clean and beautiful, and wear long-sleeved clothes so that children can sleep under the mosquito nets for our health," she said.
Sore throats in children are caused by bad weather, hot and cold, and parents' negligence on the part of the child when the child begins to have a slight fever, he did not think about this. He thought it was okay for his children. When his children had serious problems, he was sent to the hospital for treatment. It takes a little longer to heal.
"For patients who come to the hospital, the teacher is very caring, regardless of race, color or political affiliation, because the treatment of patients to save the lives of patients is the duty of his team. Doctor, doctor. Therefore, the team of doctors must adhere to all the duties of doctors who are ethical, ethical, professional in fulfilling their duties to serve the people and the country, regardless of fatigue, day or night.
"For patients who are sent to the provincial referral hospital, they are everywhere, from nearby islands, districts and provincial towns," she said. As for the service, the hospital never determines the service fee because most of our people come to the government department for treatment, most of them live in poverty. To alleviate the difficulties and solve the life of the doctors, we gave him two meals at noon and evening.
According to the parents of the child who came to the hospital, he told reporters that as a parent, he was very happy that his friend had been treated by doctors and hoped that he would recover. Heals in two or three days. He will be back home.
Dr. Hay Layson, director of the Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital, said that for the treatment of children admitted to the provincial referral hospital, not a single child died. This proves that the doctors are not negligent and follow the orders of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Health and in fulfilling their duties as doctors for society, for the people, for the nation and in accordance with the existing policy of peace. Samdech Techo is the leader.
The doctor appealed to people from all walks of life, if there is any change in health, please hurry to the hospital or health center in the commune to discuss, consult and provide information from doctors.
