After coming to work in Cambodia in 2018, Ms. Ida Unlou will end her mission in Cambodia in 2022. Before leaving Cambodia on the morning of Thursday, June 23, 2022, the Ambassador received permission from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to say goodbye and show some achievements that have been completed over the past four years.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, during the meeting, the outgoing Ambassador informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen of her efforts to improve relations and cooperation between the two countries. Cambodia and Turkey.
She emphasized that during her more than four years of mission in Cambodia, despite the fact that more than two years of Kovid 19 had spread around the world, she continued to work hard to strengthen and expand trade and political relations between the two countries. Both.
To strengthen this relationship, she has organized Samdech Techo's visit to Turkey at the end of 2018 and the next visit of senior leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia to Turkey.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen sincerely thanked and appreciated the Ambassador's great achievements in fulfilling her active diplomatic mission and bringing good results, actively contributing to the improvement of relations between Cambodia and Turkey.
Samdech Techo added that through her diplomatic mission, she has strengthened and expanded relations between Cambodia and Turkey, as well as laid many bases for strengthening and expanding economic relations between the two countries.
In this meeting, Ms. Ida Unlou also informed Samdech Techo that she was very honored to be on a mission in Cambodia to serve both Turkey and Cambodia. She stressed that working in Cambodia brings back many memories and that leaving Cambodia now makes her feel like she is leaving home.
Despite the completion of her mission in Cambodia, the Ambassador expressed her deep sympathy for helping Cambodia. In particular, make the relationship between Cambodia and Turkey stronger and deeper, no matter where she is.
In return for the Ambassador's merits and efforts during her mission in Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to award her the Maha Sereywat Co-op Medal, a high-level medal.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen personally presented the medal to her this morning. She would like to express her deep gratitude to Samdech Techo for awarding this honorary medal.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Receives Turkish Ambassador and Farewell Ceremony
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of Thursday, June 23, 2022, allowed Ms. Ayda Unlu to bid farewell after completing her mission in Cambodia.
With the permission to say goodbye, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also presented her with the Medal of Merit. The Solidarity Medal is an award honoring the Ambassador for her efforts to improve relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Turkey.
Please note that Ms. Ayda Unlu came to work as the Turkish Ambassador to Cambodia in 2018. During her four-year mission, she has worked hard to improve relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Turkey.
