(Kratie): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, emphasized that the Zero Trap Campaign not only focuses on land and air traps, but also on water traps such as: nets, traps and other fishing gear. Also, do not disturb the dolphin conservation area.
Speaking at the press conference of the Zero Trap Campaign in Kratie Provincial Protected Area last weekend, HE Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the trap is still a serious threat to all kinds of wildlife, especially wildlife and not. Cambodia is not the only country facing the problem of trapping in protected areas, and protected areas in many Asian countries are threatened by traps.
According to park rangers and conservation officials, the perpetrators now use traps by tying wires to the electric current to capture wildlife in parallel with other traps, such as cable traps, snare traps.
Chhit Kim On, a representative of the Prek Prosop Wildlife Conservation Community of the Mekong Floodplain in Kratie province, said that the traps were set up by the perpetrators to catch wild animals 10 to 20 meters long. He said that not only can kill wildlife, but also endanger human life, especially park rangers and conservation officers during patrols to enforce the law.
