Ministry of Education, in collaboration with the Fred Hollow Foundation, inspected the eye health of more than 1,000 students in Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province.
(Kampong Cham): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has partnered with the Fred Hollow Foundation in Cambodia under the auspices of USAID through UNOPS to implement a project to increase the scope of imaging services and improve the national financing model for the supply of glasses in Cambodia 2021-2023. This morning, June 22, 2022, more than 1,000 students were examined for eye health in Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province.
The ceremony was held at Hun Sen Khchao High School in Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province in the presence of Ms. Kim Sethany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and was attended by representatives of the Ministry of Health, representatives of the Free Hollow Foundation in Cambodia, representatives of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, as well as many students. Also.
On that occasion, Ms. Kim Sethany confirmed that this is the first time for Kang Meas District to have an eye health examination and provide glasses to students. After passing eye tests to more than 1,000 students, more than 30 students were found to have eye problems, and the team continued to examine them through eye examination equipment and cut glasses given to him.
Ms. Kim Sethany added that most of the eye problems that occur to students today are due to the use of multiple eyes with the phone, online learning, in particular, can also occur due to lack of awareness related. Eye care and eating foods that contain vitamins also help the eyes.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Supports Cambodian Bokator Training for Indonesian Players
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has announced his support for the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between Cambodia and Indonesia on the training of bokator martial arts to Indonesian athletes, and Indonesia to train Cambodian martial arts.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's support was made during a working meeting with Indonesian Defense Minister Prabowo Subianto on the afternoon of June 22, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, during the meeting, the Indonesian Minister of Defense informed about the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia and Indonesia for mutual training. To players between Cambodian bokator and Indonesian martial arts.
In addition to informing the signing of the memorandum, the Minister of National Defense also requested the approval of Samdech Techo. Samdech Techo Hun Sen supported the Memorandum of Understanding on Martial Arts Training. Samdech Techo considered this to be a good culture between Cambodia and Indonesia.
In this meeting, the Minister of Defense of Indonesia informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen about the results of the meeting between him and Lt. Gen. Chap Pheakdey, Commander of the 911 Special Forces. The Minister informed Samdech Techo that during the meeting, he decided to provide scholarships to Cambodian military students to study at the Indonesian National Defense School in the fields of medicine, engineering and mathematics and science.
The Prime Minister praised the cooperation between the Indonesian and Cambodian Armed Forces and thanked the Cambodian military students for providing scholarships to study in Indonesia. Samdech Techo considers this a culture of cooperation between the two countries' armies.
It should be noted that in this courtesy call with Samdech Techo, Lt. Gen. Prabowo Subianto congratulated Samdech Techo for leading Cambodia towards rapid development. The Indonesian Minister of Defense highlighted that comparing Cambodia when he visited five years ago and now is very different, that is, Cambodia has now become a beautiful developed country.
Kandal Provincial Governor Urges Authorities at All Levels and Citizens to Plant All Kinds of Trees for Common Benefits
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, urged the authorities at all levels and the people to plant all kinds of trees in resorts, pagodas, schools, villages, canals, roads and public places and try to keep them growing. Grow well to benefit all of us.
The Governor of Kandal Province made this remark while presiding over the celebration of Tree Day on July 9 and the tree planting ceremony on June 22, 2022 at Hun Sen Chey Thom Secondary School, Chey Thom Commune, Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province.
The provincial governor stated that planting all kinds of trees in order to help preserve the environment, enhance the landscape, create green shade and cool shade for teachers, students and our people, moreover, the forest is an important natural resource. In order to maintain the balance of the environment and contribute to the development of the economy, eco-tourism, ecology, culture and a safe haven for all kinds of people and animals that live on this planet.
After all, deforestation is one of the major problems in the world that is causing adverse effects on soil fertility and natural disasters such as droughts, floods, climate change, global warming, etc. Which leads to complications in the lives of people, animals and plants, especially in agriculture.
On July 9, 2022, a total of 2,800 trees were planted along Street 383, Street 383M, 14 km long, in Roka Chanleung and Chey Thom communes, Khsach Kandal district, including: Peacock Kinin and Chan Kiri. Meanwhile, the Forestry Administration also took 5,000 saplings to distribute to the people invited here.
