Indonesia expects to export chicken to Singapore soon
JAKARTA: Indonesian authorities hope to reach an agreement with Singapore to start exporting chicken in the coming weeks as Singapore seeks alternative sources after neighboring Malaysia tightens exports. Chicken. According to Reuters.
In a sign of global food shortages and worsening supply chain problems, Malaysia has halted chicken exports until domestic production and rising costs return to stability.
The ban has had a profound effect on Singapore, with restaurants and street stalls raising prices for its popular chicken dishes.
The Singapore Food Agency (SFA) said in a statement that it was "working closely" with Indonesian authorities to recognize Indonesia as a potential source of chicken imports.
The ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting, which Cambodia is hosting for 2022, was chaired by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Defense and chaired the 16th ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting.
According to a press release issued by the Ministry of Defense on June 17, 2022, the ASEAN Defense Ministers will hear a report on recent developments in ASEAN and a briefing. Outcomes of the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting as well as the adoption of new initiatives and joint declarations of the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting include:
The meeting will also consider India's proposal for ASEAN-India maritime exercises and the decision to hold an informal meeting between ASEAN defense ministers and a number of countries in November 2022.
On the occasion of the meeting, the Heads of Delegation of ASEAN Member States and the Secretary-General of ASEAN will pay a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
During the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting, informal meetings between the ASEAN-Japan Defense Ministers will be held in person and the informal meetings between the ASEAN-China Defense Ministers will be held on video format.
As the host of the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting and related security meetings in 2022, Cambodia is committed to promoting ASEAN solidarity, jointly addressing current regional security challenges and emerging challenges under the theme "Solidarity". For security and harmony. " Laos appoints new central bank governor, restricts foreign exchange sales
(VOVworld) - Laos' parliament on Monday approved the appointment of a new central bank governor and two deputy prime ministers, as the Southeast Asian nation faces a shortage of foreign exchange reserves. According to Reuters.
The Central Bank of Laos on Monday also introduced a new law requiring commercial banks and exchange counters to limit daily foreign currency sales to 15 million kip (about $ 1,002) per person, Reuters reported. Well.
The National Assembly also approved the appointment of new chairs in the Ministry of Industry and Commerce and the state audit body, Reuters reported.
On June 3, the Myanmar military announced that it would execute former lawmakers from Aung San Suu Kyi's political party and a prominent pro-democracy activist, both of whom had been convicted of terrorism. If carried out, it would be the first judicial execution for an ASEAN country since 1990.
Nicholas Koumjian, head of the UN's Independent Investigative Mechanism for Myanmar, which closely monitors the case, said: "According to the information we have gathered, it is under the law. "Internationally, the fundamental rights of these convicts are clearly violated in the court proceedings."
Koumjian added that "the death penalty or even detention for a period of time based on judicial procedures that do not meet the basic conditions of a fair trial could be tantamount to a crime." "War or crimes against humanity."
