The United States has recently seen a spate of shootings, most notably the May 25 shooting at Uvalde Elementary School in Texas, which has shocked public opinion. Twenty-one people have been killed in the largest school shooting in the United States in nearly a decade.
As of June 15, 19,841 people had been killed in a series of shootings in the United States, according to the latest figures from the US gun violence archives website. Including 752 minors, in addition to 16,799 people were injured. The latest data also shows that this year, the number of large-scale shootings in the United States has risen to 267.
But the root cause of all this is because American politicians ignore the people's right to life. At the time of the shooting at Robb Elementary School in Uvalde, US leaders were busy provoking a group rivalry in Asia. For some American politicians, the lives lost in the shootings are nothing but American personal interests and American hegemony.
No one knows how many more lives were lost by gunfire to awaken the conscience of American politicians. When they ignore the fundamental right to life of their own people, can the world believe that they will really care about the human rights of other countries? "American-style human rights" fake masks have already been shattered by gunfire.
The funny thing is that New Zealand and Canada, members of the "Five Eyes Alliance" like the United States, are very different in terms of gun control. The New Zealand government has submitted a draft law to the House of Representatives amending the gun law following the March 15, 2019 mass shootings in Christchurch, announcing a ban on the sale and possession of semi-automatic rifles, military-style and assault rifles.
We should ask, how many more lives have been lost through gunfire to awaken the conscience of American politicians? When power and capital are placed on the lives of the people, it will inevitably lead to more and more human rights tragedies.
