The following is the Royal Decree of the King: Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province Celebrates the 15th Anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day June 21, 2022
(Kampong Thom): Following the instructions of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on the morning of June 21, 2022, the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province celebrated the 15th anniversary of Veterans Day. Cambodia.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Provincial Governor and Honorary Chairman of the Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Thom Province, which was held at the Veterans' Village on a social land concession in Dangkda Village, Kraya Commune, Santuk District. Kampong Thom with 150 families of veterans.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun, Deputy Commander of the Kampong Thom Veterans Association, read out a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association on the occasion of the 15th anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day. June 21, 2022 To all veterans and compatriots.
On this occasion, Major General Som Sun would like to express his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for providing one and a half hectare social land concession to a family and a new house. To 141 families of landless veterans living in various places in Kampong Thom province came to live here.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak thanked all the veterans who sacrificed their lives for the cause of the nation and the people of Cambodia to contribute to the complete peace of our country under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
On the occasion of the 15th anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day today, I would like to pray to the angels to take care of all veterans and their families, to be happy, prosperous and to live a long life, and to send a message to our ex-family members. All fighters must take care to grow crops, grow vegetables and raise animals to improve the livelihood of each family.
Afterwards, the Honorary President of Kampong Thom Provincial Veterans Association and Stung Sen Market Traders donated some food and money to 150 families of veterans who participated in the celebration of the 15th anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day on June 21. This 2022 as well.
A tourist bus was hit by a broken tree branch at the Transfiguration Temple
(Siem Reap): A tourist bus was hit by a tree branch due to strong winds on the evening of June 20 in front of the Transfiguration Temple in North Srah Srang Village, Nokor Thom Sangkat, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
However, the broken branch hit the head of the car and immediately the driver, the tour guide and the law enforcement agency stationed at the Transfiguration Temple intervened to remove the guests as they panicked. At the same time, the four guests, all female, were also very happy for their safety, which was not injured.
