Kampong Speu Provincial Administration warns people to beware of dengue fever after the alarming outbreak, in early 2022, there were 1344 cases, an increase of more than 100%
(Kampong Speu): Kampong Speu Provincial Administration has instructed the people in the province to clean and store old motorcycle tires properly in the business of selling car tires at car repair garages to eliminate tiger mosquitoes after the Ministry of Health. Report more than 100% increase in dengue fever.
According to the provincial administration, the results of the hydrological survey combined with the weather factors that increased rainfall during the beginning of this year, dengue cases will face a sharp increase in the rainy season in villages, communes and towns of some provinces. Especially with the construction of buildings (construction sites) and a large population.
Along with this instruction, the provincial administration also showed the safe storage of car and motorcycle tires by stacking them on top of each other, covering them with boards or mosquito nets, or pouring oil on damaged machinery, discontinuing use, or filling in soil. Especially placed under the roof to prevent water from causing a source and breeding grounds for tiger mosquitoes.
Following this instruction, the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration hopes and believes that the business owners will participate in the implementation so that Kampong Speu Province is free of dengue fever.
Cambodian Entrepreneurs Launch First Mobile Entrepreneurship Training Campaign for High School Students
The "New Generation Entrepreneur" program is a training program that motivates students as well as provides them with additional information, which is a new sprout to better understand entrepreneurship and self-development in this area, which the government is focusing on and supporting.
The entrepreneurial sector contributes greatly to the national economy, which needs to be disseminated with comprehensive training in this field to help stimulate and increase the number of new entrepreneurs that Cambodian entrepreneurs expect in the future to have young entrepreneurs. Many outstanding help increase and strengthen the national economy to grow more.
The program will be held throughout the morning, trained by trainer Mr. Duong Dara, specializing in key lessons such as the importance of entrepreneurship, the basics of entrepreneurship, finding new ideas and finding new solutions. Each high school will be attended by 200 target students with an expectation of about 1,000 entrepreneurial students for the five high schools.
The location and time of the training program with the five high schools are: Bak Touk High School of Phnom Penh on June 20, Sihanoukville High School of Sihanoukville on June 27, Samdech Ov High School of Banteay Meanchey on July 4. Kampong Thom High School of Kampong Thom Province on July 11 and Hun Sen Siem Reap High School of Siem Reap Province on July 18, 2022.
