A fire broke out in nearly 40 houses in Chbar Ampov II commune, this morning the authorities handed over Red Cross donations to the victims' families
(Phnom Penh): The fire burned nearly 40 houses and completely destroyed equipment. The above fire occurred at 4:10 pm on June 20, 2022 at a point near the bank of the road, Phum Doeum Chan, Group 04, Sangkat Chbar Ampov II, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that after receiving information from residents that a fire was burning in people's houses near the bank. In Chbar Ampov II commune, he immediately ordered the fire trucks of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to intervene.
Colonel Prohm Yorn also said that during the operation, it was difficult to intervene in time due to the narrow roads, making it difficult for fire trucks to enter, and the flames spread rapidly to the house. Neighbors. However, professional forces are still trying to intervene to prevent the devil from spreading to people's homes.
Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that in the case of the above fire, the house and all the damaged equipment (3 meters by 4 meters) were built of stone, wood, and zinc. The cause of the fire was due to a house fire.
On the morning of June 21, 2022, the working group of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch in Chbar Ampov District, led by Mr. Cheng Monira, Honorary President of the Sub-Branch, visited and brought humanitarian donations to 37 fire victims. Smith and 43 families.
