Interior Ministry spokesman: 45 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on June 20
(Phnom Penh): At least 45 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on June 20, 2022 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on June 21.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 45 suspects, 20 were arrested in 14 criminal cases and 25 were arrested in 15 drug cases.
Ministry of Environment calls on all stakeholders to make Prek Prosop Wildlife Sanctuary safer for deer
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, called on the people living in the area around Prek Prosop Wildlife Sanctuary to cooperate with the authorities and partner organizations to make the Prek Prosop Wildlife Sanctuary safer for animals. Deer prevent encroachment on forest land, especially eliminate all kinds of traps.
Neth Pheaktra made the call during a press visit to the Mekong Delta on Thursday 16 June 2022 by WWF and released a report on the situation of deer in Cambodia.
On that occasion, a senior official of the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the research shows that a total of 84 deer are living in the Prek Prosop Wildlife Sanctuary of Kratie Province, which shows the global value of the Mekong floodplain landscape. For the conservation of deer, the rarest species for the universe. Deer survival is threatened by habitat loss, poaching and the trap crisis caused by the illegal wildlife trade.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stressed that urgent joint conservation measures are important and necessary to protect the endangered deer's final habitat, ensuring that its natural habitat is free of traps and stopping the demand for wildlife meat and animal products. Forests to restore the number of deer and other species and to be able to survive in the wild in the future.
According to Eam Sam Onn, WWF Director of the Mekong Biodiversity Survey and Monitoring Unit: "Cambodia is the first country in the world to conserve this rare species."
Mr. Seng Teak, Director of WWF, said that the current findings not only highlighted Cambodia's reputation on the international stage, but also highlighted the global importance of the Mekong landscape as an important habitat for survival. Of wildlife, both on land and in water of all kinds.
He added: "WWF appreciates and thanks the efforts of the park rangers and law enforcement officials, with the active participation of local authorities and communities in protecting these wildlife areas. The benefits of nature and all generations.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized: "The Ministry of Environment encourages people living around protected areas to participate in the conservation of natural resources and biodiversity by abandoning hunting and trapping, stop buying wildlife meat to participate in the care and conservation. "Rare species like this deer for the benefit of this generation and future generations in the long run and to strengthen the livelihood development of local communities."
Researchers will continue to strengthen the scientific data on deer deployment, using advanced drone technology with thermal cameras throughout the sanctuary.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inspected the construction of National Road No. 71C (Tbong Khmum-Chamkar Leu), completed 37%
(Tbong Khmum): After being invited to celebrate the 45th anniversary of the march towards the overthrow of the genocidal regime, on the afternoon of June 20, 2022, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Inspected the construction of National Road No. 71C connecting Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province to Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province, which is more than 114 kilometers long.
The construction inspection was also attended by the leadership of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, technical officers, representatives of construction companies, technical inspection companies, local authorities and stakeholders.
The purpose of this inspection is to inspect the technical characteristics, monitor the progress of the construction work and check whether the construction company is carrying out each work correctly according to the load book or contract to ensure the quality of the road, strong and durable.
In addition, the Senior Minister instructed the construction company and the construction technical inspection company to pay attention to the construction based on the principle of quality first and to water regularly so as not to disturb and affect the health of passengers and you. People living along that road.
The Senior Minister also requested the transport companies as well as the people not to carry more than the legal limit of goods, which will damage the road. The minister outlined the formula for overweight and quickly damaged roads, so that a truck carrying more than 10 tons is equivalent to 10,000 trucks on the road. If one truck carries more than 30 tons, it is equivalent to 81,000 vehicles driving on the road.
According to a report by the General Technical Department of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the construction of National Road 71C has so far reached 37 percent.
Please note that National Road No. 71C is a potential national economic artery of Cambodia, can facilitate communication, integration, interconnection within the country and with the region, contribute to improving the efficiency of trade, investment, crop. Agro-industry and tourism are fast and low cost, especially with neighboring countries.
The road is scheduled to take 42 months to complete, with completion scheduled for October 2024. The road is being built by Shanghai Construction Company (SCG) and technically inspected by Guangzhou Wanan Technical Consulting, with a construction cost of nearly $ 130 million.
