(Stung Treng): At the moment, teams from other countries are monitoring the movement of 300 kilograms of freshwater giant trout to find out more and to better protect them.
One of the great mysteries of wildlife for a long time is that the identity of the world's largest freshwater fish species seems to have been revealed last week as fishermen in northern Cambodia work. International scientists have discovered a 300-kilogram freshwater giant trout near a remote island in the Mekong River.
For Zeb Hogan, a fish biologist at the University of Nevada in Reno and director of the Mekong River Miracle Project, the discovery of the giant trout is proof that the natural world can still provide new and amazing discoveries. And many of the largest aquatic species have yet to be adequately studied.
In collaboration with the Cambodian Fisheries Administration, the Mekong River Wonder Project has established a network of fishermen who agree to report the capture of endangered species of giant fish, including giant trout. Last month, fishermen in the same area reported to the team that they had caught more than 180 kilograms of female trout, which researchers then rescued back into the river.
"Now the fishermen have partnered with our project, once they catch the giant trout, we will be able to equip them and release them," said Chea Seila, project manager for the Mekong River Miracle Project. Back. These successful releases underscore the importance of our partnership with the local community. At the same time, we all have an important role to play in monitoring and conserving fisheries resources. ”
