(Svay Rieng): The project "Khmer Farm Chicken Processing Enterprise for National Pride of Cambodia", which is being implemented with 52 farming communities in 11 provinces, has been strengthening production and expanding more markets to accelerate the growth of Khmer farm chicken production and increase revenue. Income for farming families.
To help the production of this Cambodian chicken farm to grow, Heifer International Cambodia has raised an additional grant of 431,950 US dollars, with the contribution of the agricultural community to invest in the purchase of 3 vehicles transporting agricultural products, market project. 1 agricultural community, 3 tractors, 1 motorbike and 14 veterinary equipment in the farming community.
Currently, Heifer Cambodia has purchased three tractors to supply two agricultural communities in Svay Rieng and one in Battambang. The three tractors were handed over to the agricultural community on June 20, 2022 at the office of Men Chey Samaki Svay Chek Agricultural Community in Men Chey village, Men Chey commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province.
Dr. Nhem Sareth, country director of Heifer International Cambodia, said the tractor would help fill a labor shortage in the farming community and attract young people to return to farming. In addition, it can also provide additional income to the farming community by providing rental services to community members.
He said that Heifer Cambodia has contributed to strengthen and improve the production of agricultural products and increase income for farmers' families through training and investment to implement agribusiness activities focusing on the production chain of Khmer chicken farming. Safe vegetables and expand new projects in the future.
The PPNP / PPNP project aims to accelerate the growth of Khmer chicken production through investment in agricultural community empowerment and capacity building of agricultural community institutions, as well as investment in the construction of Khmer chicken processing enterprises, farm building Incubation of standard farm chickens and investment support for smallholder farmers leading to the establishment of small and medium-sized agricultural enterprises.
The project extends the activities of the past program implementation of Heifer International Cambodia since 1999, which organized 151,089 to 300,000 smallholder families by 2030 to become self-help groups, the Union Agricultural Community. Agricultural communities in order to improve the value chain of Khmer chicken and safe vegetable production.
The program will directly benefit 151,089 farming families by 2026 in 11 provinces, which will generate more income for farming families and contribute significantly to increasing the supply of eggs, chickens, broilers. And processing and packaging of local Khmer farm chickens and reducing chicken imports from neighboring countries.
To achieve the project of Khmer Farm Chicken Processing Enterprise Project for National Pride of Cambodia, Heifer International Cambodia has organized 5 main chains, including: Farmers' families producing Khmer farm chicken eggs for hatching, building standard farm hatcheries. The family of farmers who produce chickens for meat builds enterprises to process Khmer farm chicken products, marketing and distribution of Khmer farm chickens for meat.
China's oil imports from Russia up 55% more than Saudi Arabia
SINGAPORE: China's crude oil imports from Russia rose 55 percent in May from a year earlier to an all-time high as Saudi Arabia became the largest oil supplier. Most to China. According to Reuters.
The increase comes as Chinese refiners take advantage of lower sales amid sanctions on Moscow over the invasion of Ukraine.
Reuters reports, citing data from the Chinese Customs Administration, that Russia's oil imports, including supply through pipelines in the Siberian East Pacific and by sea from Russia's European and Far Eastern ports, total. Nearly 8.42 million tons.
Saudi Arabia became the second-largest supplier in May, up 9 percent from a year earlier to 7.82 million tonnes, or 1.84 million barrels, according to Reuters. One day. That's down from 2.17 million barrels a day in April this year. Russia has overtaken Saudi Arabia as the largest supplier of oil to China from Saudi Arabia, which has held the position for 19 months.
China imported 260,000 tons of crude oil from Iran last month, the third-largest export of Iranian oil since December last year, Chinese customs data released on Monday also showed. .
China's total crude oil imports rose nearly 12 percent in May from a low of last year to 10.8 million barrels a day, compared with an average of 10.3 million barrels in 2021. According to Reuters.
