BEIJING, June 20 (Xinhua) - The Fengtai Railway Station in Beijing, China, officially resumed operations after a four-year overhaul after a halt in 2010.
Beijing Fengtai Railway Station, built in 1895, is Beijing's first station after major renovations and expansion, becoming the largest railway station in Asia with an area of about 400,000 square meters. The high-speed train has 32 lines at the same time and a capacity of nearly 20,000 passengers per hour.
Green and low-carbon features of the station, through the absorption of natural light and the use of solar panels, the station will save 950,000 kilowatts of electricity per year and reduce carbon emissions by 900 tons per year. .
