(Phnom Penh): The police force of Kambol District Inspectorate, while patrolling, found two young men standing on a suspicious street, arrested them and took them for questioning immediately.
At that time, the suspects confessed that they, together with another faction, a total of three people, acted to seize a mobile phone from a woman on June 13, 2022 at around 6:30 pm.
According to the Kambol district police report, the three suspects were: Hun Hong, 18, and Mov Theara, 19, and Hun Heng, 19. All three of them have drugs in their bodies and live in a house with no number on the road in Thmat Pong village, Sangkat Boeung Thom, Khan Kambol.
According to the report, the suspects snatched the phone from an unidentified woman on National Road 4 in front of the Tela gas station in Snguon Pich village, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kambol at around 6:30 pm. June 13, 2022. She then fled the scene, while the victim did not file a complaint, but after the incident, she also left the scene and disappeared.
The same source said that until June 16, 2022, the police of Kambol district patrolled and found two suspects, Hun Hong and Mov Theara, standing in front of the house at Thmat Pong village, Boeung Thom commune. At that time, he was taken to the Kantouk Administrative Police Station for questioning. However, the police did not immediately receive a confession from the two men.
It was not until June 17, 2022, that the two suspects confessed that they, along with another faction member, Hun Heng, had shocked a woman with a mobile phone in front of the Tela gas station in Snguon village. Pich, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kambol, on the evening of June 13.
