(Phnom Penh): Mr. Huy Vatharo, President of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, affirmed the strength of the insurance sector in Cambodia and told people not to worry about compensation, emphasizing that insurance companies in Cambodia are financially strong. An object that can fulfill its obligations.
What is the confidence for insurance users when giving money to an insurance company and when having trouble getting a refund? According to Mr. Huy Vataro, the insurance sector is under the control of the authorities with clear and proper regulations.
"Insurers are required to comply with regulations issued by the Insurance Regulatory Authority of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority to refer to one of the principles that ensures that all insurers are strong," he said. "Financially able to fulfill its obligations in the future."
Huy Vataro emphasizes that customers who purchase insurance are protected, which means that when something happens to be reimbursed, there must be a clear strategy for the insurance company to reimburse the customer.
In addition, he stated that every purchase of insurance under the insurance policy always shows a list of what risks are covered in the insurance contract and if there is a risk in accordance with what. Depending on the terms of the contract, there must be additional information related to the claim.
Meanwhile, Huy Vataro said that when a self-insured person buys life insurance and helps with the unfortunate loss of life, there is always a replacement in the policy, so when he buys the life insurance policy. Life, tell the recipient instead.
Even if the beneficiary does not know one of the principles of the insurance company, always try to find a good reason to pay, and generally the insurance company does not try to find a reason not to pay, which is the policy and professionalism of each insurance company. ⁇. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Huy Wataro.
It should be noted that the insurance premiums that the insurance group paid to customers in 2021 was US $ 41.2 million, including US $ 10.6 million in life insurance premiums (approximately US $ 8.3 million in death insurance), and insurance premiums. General $ 29.7 million and micro insurance premiums of $ 760,000.
To date, there are 39 companies that provide direct insurance services, divided into 3 categories, including: general insurance companies 18 companies, life insurance companies 14 companies, micro insurance companies 7 One company and one sub-insurance group.
In addition to the insurance companies, there are insurance brokers who provide services on behalf of the insurance companies, with 18 insurance brokers, 31 insurance agencies, of which 27 are banking and financial institutions that provide insurance agency services.
