(Phnom Penh): In a roundtable discussion on the 45th anniversary of the march towards the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot (June 20, 1977-June 20, 2022), which was held on June 19, 2022 Expertise encourages Cambodian children to study their own history clearly and together to prevent a repeat of history, especially this brutal genocidal regime.
During the roundtable discussion, Puy Kea, a correspondent for the Japan Kyodo News Agency in Cambodia, who is also an expert in political science, said that those who know history clearly can prevent bad history from happening again. Therefore, he urged Cambodian children to learn history clearly in order to be valued by those around them and have a pacifist mindset.
Puy Kea also told the next generation to learn from the previous generation because all generations can not be separated.
"People who know the history, those who know the story, that makes the debate worthwhile," he said. That is why in this context, the youth of this generation and the youth of the previous generation can not be separated, meaning that the youth of this age know the technology, but his experience can not know like the old through experience.
The veteran journalist also said that if the country fell into war like in the past, it would not be easy for any country to intervene, meaning that only Cambodians like Samdech Techo Hun Sen would sacrifice for Cambodia. For example. He added that in international relations there are only interests.
In addition, Mr. Nuon Pharath, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC), expressed the view that the value of peace is indescribable. "When it comes to peace, there are two things: a country will fall apart when there is no peace, but a country can prosper and develop if there is peace," he said.
Meanwhile, Dr. Diep Sophal, Professor of Political History of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, highly values democracy, as the Royal Government has always adopted. He sees that our country, which fell in the past due to war and after the war, our country has adopted a proper regime.
He urged people to have a national conscience and value human resources to continue to uphold democracy and escape war. The expert also criticized some individuals who caused anarchy during such a peaceful nation.
"Our experience of falling into a tragedy is that we adhere to a dictatorship," he said. Therefore, from now on, only democracy is good. We must promote national resources. "It is this national resource that serves democracy, not anarchy."
