Understand the law: work permits and work books for foreigners
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia, as the rule of law, has authorized a labor law issued by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to provide for foreign workers wishing to come to work in Cambodia.
For this week, Fresh News 'Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "Foreigners' work permits and workbooks" to explain and share to the following students.
Work permits and work permits for foreigners are issued to workers who come to work in the Kingdom of Cambodia, and this work permit and work book is made for the purpose of identifying and identifying the type of occupation that is allowed to work in the Kingdom. Cambodia.
In the spirit of Article 261 of the Labor Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, it states that no foreigner can engage in any business without a work permit and a work permit issued by the Ministry of Labor.
To obtain a work permit and work book, the applicant must meet the following conditions:
A. Employers must have a valid work permit in order to conduct their business in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
B. The foreigner has entered the Kingdom of Cambodia legally.
E. The foreigner must be physically fit for the job and not have any infectious diseases. This condition is determined by a Prakas of the Ministry of Health with the approval of the Ministry in charge of Labor.
The Occupational Physician will then issue a physical examination certificate for use because when applying for a work permit and workbook, the physical examination certificate must be accompanied by the following attachments:
After the application is completed, the owner of the factory must wait for 20 (twenty) days after the application is completed. Occupation and labor of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
Separately for factories in the provinces can be taken at the Department of Labor and Vocational Training in that province. On the other hand, in the case of any factory or enterprise that hires foreign workers without a work permit and work book, that factory and enterprise shall be liable before the law and shall be punished in accordance with the law in force of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
