Senior officials of the Ministry of Education set out 8-point plan for the Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Education and provincial schools to continue to implement
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Chea Cheat, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, aims to continue the eight-point work activities for the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Svay Rieng Province, as well as schools throughout the province to continue to implement effectively.
This action plan was presented at the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of the academic year 2020-2021 and to set the direction for further activities of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Svay Rieng Province on the afternoon of June 17, 2022.
The meeting to review the work results of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Svay Rieng Province also has some challenges such as:
* Some schools have not yet become development-friendly schools, and some teachers still do not use lesson plans and process materials for teaching.
School management and a small number of teachers are not yet fully involved in professional development as teachers.
* Secondary and high school dropout rates remain high.
* Some schools still lack school buildings and some are so dilapidated that students are not allowed to attend school.
In order to contribute to the development of education, youth and sports, Mr. Chea Cheat urged all relevant officials to participate in some important work for the new school year as follows:
1: Continue to strengthen education services to ensure quality, equity and environment, as well as promote lifelong learning for all and address the learning of students and youth in need.
2: Continue to promote "clean environment, good service" "Good management, good teaching, good learning" by continuing to maintain, improve, repair, build school buildings and equip adequate furniture, pay attention to build libraries, laboratories, workshops, home rooms, gardens. Vegetables, biodiversity gardens, sports fields.
3: Continue to promote the participation of parents, guardians, community students to help monitor their children's education and help develop schools.
4: Continue to develop the management and leadership capacity of education officials at all levels, reform of teacher training, and professional development of teachers.
5: Continue to develop digital education through the integration of digital technology at all levels, curricula equipped with digital laboratories in educational institutions, enhance the capacity of digital teachers and disseminate this work widely.
6: Continue to be more active in the work of scouts and youth by adhering to good deeds in society by inspiring good children, good students, good friends, good citizens, youth volunteer programs in the community with the training of technical skills and soft skills for young people. To respond in a timely manner to job opportunities in society.
7: Continue to improve health and hygiene in educational institutions by paying attention to school sales.
8: Continue to improve environmental education, planting trees in the school yard in the classroom and waste management, exercise, support the physical and mental health of students.
