Twelve Cambodian students receive scholarships to study in Japan
(Phnom Penh): The Embassy of Japan in Cambodia on June 17, 2022 organized a ceremony to send 12 Cambodian high school students who received scholarships to study in Japan through the Kakehashi Asia Scholarship Program 2022.
The event was attended by Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, Mr. Youk Ngoy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Seang Mol, Deputy Director of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center, as well as parents and alumni of Asia Kakashi Scholarship and All 5th generation students as well.
Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, congratulated all the 5th generation students who received this Asia Kakashi Scholarship.
The Japanese ambassador said that the Asia Kakashi Scholarship was started in 2018 with the aim of training human resources who will become a bridge of friendship in Asia. In 2022, Japan plans to accept 250 high school students from 20 countries and regions in Asia to study at high schools across Japan as foreign students, including 12 high school students from Cambodia.
He said that so far, 37 Cambodian high school students have gone to study in Japan through this scholarship. This time, he heard that the children would go to high schools across Japan from Hokkaido to Miyazaki prefecture.
He believes that students who have been awarded this difficult scholarship will have no more problems and will gain new experiences in each area and create great memories. He claimed that international students from Cambodia so far have been positive, friendly and have a good reputation. High schools that used to accept Cambodian students are likely to be applying for Cambodian students again.
In addition, the Ambassador of Japan would like to thank the parents of all the students who have supported their children's aspirations so that they can have a new experience in Japan. He believes that the experience of studying abroad and living in Japan will surely expand the understanding of all students as well as provide capital for the future.
