Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Asks US Companies to Invest in Cambodia's Transportation Sector
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has asked the US team to invest in the transport sector in Cambodia, which Cambodia is working to improve so that transportation costs are cheaper and less time consuming.
The Minister's request was made at the opening ceremony of the Vehicle Technical Training Center on Friday morning, June 17, 2022. This vehicle technology training center was established in collaboration with Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and RMA Group. The center provides free training.
At the inauguration of the center, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, has launched a master plan to improve and develop the transportation sector to make transportation costs cheaper in Cambodia. Before and use less time can compete with neighboring countries or countries in the region to attract more investors to invest in Cambodia.
According to Sun Chanthol, the master plan for the development of the transportation sector consists of about 330 projects, with an investment budget of about 50 billion US dollars and a development period of 10 years.
To bring the transportation development plan to fruition, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol asked Ford, RMA to help attract more US investors to participate in the implementation of logistics investment development in Cambodia. This.
