(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, on June 17, 2022, confirmed the preparation of necessary measures to support Cambodia's economic growth and maintain financial stability. Which is the main priority.
Her confirmation was made during the dissemination workshop on the Financial Stability Report 2021 organized by the National Bank of Cambodia.
She said the Cambodian economy is expected to grow at around 5% by 2022, mainly supported by exports of agricultural products, transport, telecommunications and improved investment flows and remittances. From abroad.
Cambodia has now reopened the country with no travel restrictions due to high vaccination rates and no alarming new infections. In terms of trade and investment, Cambodia is expected to benefit from the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), the Bilateral Free Trade Agreement and the introduction of a new investment law.
However, the spread of Kovid-19 has not yet ended, and the risk of a new, potentially serious mutation virus continues to spread.
She added that the Russia-Ukraine war and China's packaging measures have been putting pressure on global economic growth. Inflation is already high due to an imbalance in demand and supply caused by the Kovid-19 epidemic and the effects of the Russia-Ukraine war.
The situation has prompted central banks in developed countries to raise interest rates to curb the emergence of inflation, which could put emerging and developing economies facing tightening financial conditions, capital outflows and exchange rate pressures.
"In this challenging situation, the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to closely monitor the progress of the Cambodian banking system and the economy as a whole and be ready to take the necessary steps to support national economic growth while maintaining financial stability," she added. The main priority work.
She said the banking system remains strong and can provide the necessary credit to support economic activity. During 2021, assets and deposits of the banking system increased by 18% and 17.7%, respectively, and loans increased by 23.5%.
