Ms. Seng Chantheary and 42 other activists on June 14, 2022 were sentenced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to 6 years in prison for inciting and conspiracy under Articles 453, 494 and 495 of the Penal Code. Cambodia is involved in leading, supporting and participating in the November 9 event, an illegal plot to overthrow the legitimate government under the guise of Sam Rainsy's return in 2019.
In this case, the spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice recalled the following aspects of the facts and aspects of the law related to the events of November 9:
1: On the facts of the events related to the events of November 9, what is behind the plan for the return of Sam Rainsy on November 9, 2019? In 2019, everyone may remember that under the plan to return to Cambodia on November 9, 2019 can be called "Event 9/11", Sam Rainsy and his accomplices carried out many activities that can gather There are 3 major activities as follows:
(1): Incited and appealed to the Armed Forces and civil servants to revolt against the Royal Government
(Second): Incited and called on the people to revolt against the government
(Third): Raise and raise funds to raise illegal forces to carry out the above activities.
2: Legal aspects related to the events of November 9:
From a legal point of view, is there any country in the world that does not consider the plot to attempt the coup or the plan to overthrow the legitimate government violently as illegal and to exercise the right to freedom? Some countries even consider these groups to be terrorist organizations. Therefore, we can conclude that:
* It is only right that the Royal Government put in place the necessary measures as an independent and sovereign state, including legal, political and diplomatic measures, to completely destroy the plan to destroy Cambodia led by prisoner Sam Rainsy. And factions and ensure the maintenance of peace, stability and peace of the people.
* It is only right that countries around the world do not support the illegal plans of Sam Rainsy and his cronies and have contributed significantly to the failure of the plan to destroy the peace, security and stability of Cambodia led by Sam Rainsy and his cronies. Shame.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Justice further stated that the above decision is a decision of the court, which is an independent power stated and guaranteed by the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. According to Cambodian law, a person who does not agree with the lower court's decision has the right to appeal to the higher court and has the right to find a lawyer in accordance with the laws and procedures in force.
