According to the Directive on the Preparation of the Draft Financial Law for 2023, issued by the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the industry as a whole will continue to grow at a rate of 9.2% in 2023, which is returning. Towards the growth trend before the Kovid 19 crisis, supported by the continued improvement of external demand, which will boost the garment sub-sector and non-garment manufacturing.
The garment sub-sector is projected to continue to achieve strong growth of 8.1% in 2023, supported by the stabilization of domestic factors achieved through higher vaccination rates of workers, the improvement of External factors, in particular, anticipate continued growth in demand from the US and EU markets and continued diversification of orders from countries in the region, especially Myanmar.
However, the garment sub-sector may continue to face challenges such as increased competition from neighboring countries, loss of diversion orders, uncertainty over preferential tariffs and limited use of technology. In production.
He said that for orders this year, in the first three months, there was a good growth of about 30%. He expects orders to maintain strong growth by 2023. However, he also worries about some of the challenges hindering the sector.
He worries that the sector will also face risks in the future as Cambodia will face saturation of the garment sector.
He explained that we have been sewing since 1996 for more than 36 years, and therefore Cambodia must be ready to shift its production shift from labor-intensive to technology-intensive industries. Its labor force to leave the plant sector, which can diversify a lot of production.
