(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, stated that Buddhism teaches people to live in peace and respect each other, therefore, Samdech asked to preserve the values of Buddhism.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said this on the afternoon of June 17, 2022 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall during the dedication ceremony of "Abhich Chhak Moha Sathom Chotak" to Samdech Preah Akka Moha Sangkha, President of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Dr. Tep Vong, Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Presented by the State Council of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that the Cambodian Constitution has historically recorded that Buddhism is the state religion, based on the reason that about 90% of Cambodians adopt Buddhism, adopt Buddhism as a way of life, become a soul, a national identity and a foundation. A repository of Khmer culture.
Samdech continued that Buddhism has played an active role in contributing to the development of the nation in terms of economy, environment, education, morality and behavior in Cambodian society until it has become a solid foundation in supporting the entire national civilization and culture. In this spirit, the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided full support to Buddhism from the past to the present to ensure the prosperity and strength of Buddhism in parallel with the realm of empire.
