Banteay Srei District Forestry Administration is looking for criminals to steal rosewood trees and provide $ 1,000 for informants
(Siem Reap): The Banteay Srei District Forestry Administration is searching for the culprit who stole four rosewood trees from a 50-year-old rosewood plantation.
Mr. Mong Bunlim said that in the villages around the area of rosewood plantations, his expertise has submitted a request to the provincial commissioner to spy on the villages and have a network from the people to the regional forces and cooperate with all authorities. Rank from village to commune to find the perpetrators and bring them to justice.
Four rosewood trees, about 50 years old, were stolen by unidentified criminals in an 1880-hectare rosewood plantation in Khnat Po village and Wat village, Sre Po commune, Varin district, Khna Krao commune. Kantuot, Svay Leu district and Khun Ream commune, Banteay Srey district, Siem Reap province.
With this, Mr. Mong Bunlim appealed to the public who know the news related to the perpetrators and reported and provided information to the authorities to arrest the perpetrators, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Siem Reap will give a reward of 1,000 Dollars (one thousand US dollars) and the information is kept confidential so that there is no problem for the above informants.
