The directive states that the war between Russia and Ukraine had an indirect effect on the Cambodian economy through the increase in prices of all kinds of goods, especially fuel and agricultural raw materials, including fertilizers and pesticides. At the same time, the overall increase in prices has affected domestic spending and consumption, as well as people's daily lives.
However, the impact of the war on the Cambodian economy was small due to the low level of direct economic relations between Cambodia and the two conflicting countries, which was largely offset by the achievement. The high rate of Kovid-19 vaccination has made Cambodia a community-based immunity, a key basis for the country's reopening, and has allowed local economic activity to return to normal.
The agricultural sector is projected to grow at around 1.1% in 2023 due to strong growth in the livestock and crop sub-sectors, while the fisheries sub-sector is expected to continue to recover slowly. Livestock sub-sector is expected to grow around 1.0%, crop sub-sector is expected to grow 1.6% and fishery sub-sector is expected to grow 0.6%.
The industrial sector is projected to continue to grow at a rate of 9.2% in 2023, returning to the pre-Kovid-19 crisis, supported by a continued improvement in external demand. Boost the growth of the garment sub-sector by 8.1%, the non-garment manufacturing sub-sector by 13.3% and the construction sub-sector by 7.2%.
In 2022, inflation is projected to rise to around 5.0% due to high international oil and other commodity prices caused by the war between Russia and Ukraine. For 2023, inflation is expected to slow to around 2.5% due to the expectation of a return to normal prices of oil and other commodities, as well as economic activity.
The exchange rate is expected to average around 4,065 riel per US dollar in 2022 and 2023 due to the intervention of the National Bank of Cambodia to maintain price stability and public confidence in the use of the riel.
(Phnom Penh): On June 16, 2022, the Press and Quick Reaction Unit of the Office of the Council of Ministers released an official video, lasting about 15 minutes, with English translation and subtitles entitled " Why do Cambodians continue to give so much confidence to the CPP government? ”
This video highlights the great success of the election process as well as the results of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election on June 5, 2022 recently.
The 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 is another turning point in the history of the multi-party liberal democracy process in the Kingdom of Cambodia. The Cambodian people went to the polls to vote for the Cambodian People's Party in a landslide, which resulted in the ruling party led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen winning an overwhelming majority.
According to preliminary results, the CPP controls almost all of the 1,488 commune chiefs out of 1,652 communes nationwide.
The CPP also won commune councilors out of 11,622 councilors. This is a result of the unwavering popularity and strength of the Cambodian People's Party, which continues to provide people with greater confidence and trust.
