Minister of Information Questioning Court Reaction to Prosecution of "Seng Theary" for Implementing "Freedom of Expression" Standard
(Phnom Penh): Minister of Information Khieu Kanharith has questioned the implementation of the "Freedom of Expression" standard to countries and human rights organizations that have reacted to the Cambodian court's sentencing of Ms. Seng Theary, a Cambodian-American, to prison. .
On June 14, 2022, Seng Theary was sentenced by a Phnom Penh Municipal Court judge to six years in prison for conspiracy and incitement to cause serious social unrest. The allegations come after a court found that Seng Theary was involved in an attempt to overthrow the government through a "November 9 plan" organized by Sam Rainsy, an illegal rebel movement.
Hours after the Phnom Penh Municipal Court's verdict, the US Embassy in Cambodia was the first to react, followed by Western countries and a number of human rights organizations.
Through his Facebook page this morning, June 16, 2022, the Minister of Information does not seem to be surprised by these reactions, because it is a reaction as he intended.
"As I said before! "Immediately, the Cambodian court convicted his nephew, Mr. Sharp Nose, Sharp Nose, and Silo from Sharp Nose, shouting about freedom of expression." This is the highlight of the Minister of Information.
In response to the reaction of countries claiming to be the fathers of democracy respecting freedom of expression, the Minister of Information recalled his questions posed to all countries regarding the implementation of their measures on the country's media. Russia after the war between Russia and Ukraine.
Regarding the Russia-Ukraine war, Minister Khieu Kanharith stated that Cambodia opposes Russia's invasion of Ukraine based on the principles stated by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia opposes any threat of force and use of force in Every solution between one country and another.
Seeing the biased practice of freedom of expression that the United States and the West, as well as some human rights groups have memorized, Khieu Kanharith raised the question of whether they use the same scale in "freedom." Of expression »or not?
Through these gestures, it is clear that their appreciation of freedom of expression does not meet universal standards.
