The US Department of Energy said the distribution of crude oil from the Strategic Reserve (SPR) sale will run from Aug. 16 to Sept. 30.
Reuters reports that the release of oil from the stockpile aims to help control rising oil prices after Russia, one of the world's largest oil producers, invaded Ukraine and as the West imposed sanctions. On Moscow.
Brent crude has risen sharply since Biden announced the release on March 31, trading above $ 120 a barrel. The rise comes as some of the world's oil producers cut back on oil production as the epidemic boosts demand for oil.
U.S. government officials say oil prices could have been higher if there had been no release from reserves. But the release also pushed stockpiles to their lowest level since 1987, raising concerns about a tight global oil market despite the United States having more oil reserves. Requirements under international agreements.
