Regarding the export of products to China, Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that if you look at the export figures between China and Cambodia, there is still a trade deficit. That is, exports from Cambodia to China are still low, while imports to China are still high.
He added that Cambodia, as a developing country, usually has a demand for a variety of goods, especially raw materials from superpowers to produce for export.
He added that the signing of a free trade agreement between China and Cambodia shows that Cambodia is one step ahead of many international trade partners in the region and the world. Therefore, Cambodia needs to increase the production of goods that China needs and cooperate with Chinese companies to produce and export more to this country, especially agricultural goods.
