General knowledge: Drugs helped Hitler's army win consecutive wars at the start of World War II
In fact, it was not only Germany that used tonics during World War II, even the Japanese, American, and British armies used the same type of amphetamine, but Germany was the most active user. First on the battlefield, especially in the early stages of the war.
In the face of growing concerns about the possibility of addiction and the negative effects of overuse, the German military began to reduce the distribution of peritoneum in the late 1940s, and its use declined sharply. In 1941 and 1942. However, it was still used by German troops during World War II.
