According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on June 15, 2022, the information technology nursery business registration system is a sharp reform package of the Royal Government of Cambodia in order to enhance competitiveness. And improve the business and investment environment in Cambodia.
To date, the preparation of this system has already had two phases, the first phase has been officially launched for the past two years, from June 15, 2020 to the 15th. June 2022.
The first phase is a chain registration with the Ministry of Commerce, the General Department of Taxation and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, and in the case of qualified investment projects, businesses can also apply for registration with the Council for the Development of Cambodia. .
However, the Royal Government of Cambodia has turned the crisis into an opportunity by further integrating the adoption of digital technology for service recipients and service providers to provide efficient and transparent digital public services.
In fact, the transmission of Kovid-19 into the community has begun to become tense, requiring Cambodia to close down Phnom Penh and Takhmao in Kandal province and impose a series of curfews in April and May 2021. Allows businesses to register their regular business from anywhere, completely online, and document inspectors can continue to work normally without interruption.
This modernization of public services can be done with the Cambodian Data Exchange Nursery (or CamDX) as the backbone of the operation, which the Royal Government has just issued Sub-Decree No. 164 on Data Exchange through the Nursery. Cambodia data changed at the end of August 2021.
Meanwhile, the feedback mechanism was also launched to the public in February 2022 to receive feedback to improve the use of the system. In addition, and as a national pride, Cambodia's business registration system has received attention and has been discussed in many programs, both nationally and internationally, to share experiences with other countries on the digital revolution. Of Cambodia as well.
