KOICA to Provide Third Year Online Training on "Capacity Building on Mechanisms for the Promotion and Protection of Human Rights in Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia has launched an online training program on "Capacity Building on Mechanisms for the Promotion and Protection of Human Rights in Cambodia" with the participation of participants. From the Cambodian Human Rights Committee.
The purpose of this training is to contribute to the achievement of the administrative capacity of the working class officials of the Human Rights Committee. This year, KOICA organized the third year of online training on "Capacity Building on Mechanisms for the Promotion and Protection of Human Rights in Cambodia" from 20 to 29 June 2022.
The 10-day online training course is for 20 technical officers from the Cambodian Human Rights Committee.
This important training course is designed to: First, provide references to Korea's experience in improving human rights in Cambodia, and second, assisting in the improvement and modernization of peace and security. Human Rights Education, Third: Strengthen the capacity of civil servants of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to strengthen human rights policy.
In Cambodia, KOICA works on a wide range of technical aspects of programs and projects that have a significant impact on Cambodia's development, such as improving nutrition and student well-being, capacity building of teachers, public health, agriculture, and infrastructure. KOICA will continue to support and implement programs in Cambodia that focus on human resource development.
Cambodians only saw and celebrated the event on television. Fortunately, due to the peace and development factors that have been difficult to achieve, in 2022, Cambodia has been selected by the World Football Federation as one of 51 countries in the World Cup march towards The tournament takes place in Doha, Qatar at the end of 2022.
The World Cup, which is a precious trophy and a desire to see, want to touch, want to hold for the countries of the world, also arrived in Cambodia on Wednesday morning, June 15, 2022. The arrival of the world-famous trophy made of pure gold, weighing up to 6 kg, has attracted the attention of Cambodians of all walks of life and all ages, especially football lovers.
The presence of the World Cup on Cambodian soil was warmly welcomed by the Cambodian people. In particular, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, personally received the award, which promotes the development of this football field.
This World Cup is not something that anyone can touch or lift. The procession to Cambodia, the trophy must also have the strictest security arrangements and also not open to free access. Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the only Cambodian citizen organized by the World Football Federation to raise this award.
Restricting the exposure of the trophy in order to maintain the security of the trophy and also to maintain the universal value of this trophy. Through this organized program, Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the first Cambodian citizen to touch, lift and kiss the trophy of this World Cup.
Cambodia is a country that has suffered a decline in its prestige and popularity due to the devastation caused by the crisis of war. The win-win policy of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has put an end to the flames of war in Cambodia and the current strong development.
Ending the flames of war, Cambodia's economic growth has enhanced Cambodia's honor and dignity. Cambodia has also become a hotspot for political, economic and sports events. Obviously, the World Cup parade to Cambodia would not have been possible if Cambodia were in a war crisis like in the past.
Therefore, the presence of the World Cup in Cambodia now brings a new honor and pride for the Cambodian nation. Speaking at the welcoming ceremony of the World Cup, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech is really proud like many heads of state and government to hold and raise this meaningful World Cup.
Samdech Techo also highlighted that the presence of the World Cup in Cambodia now is a testament to the world and more than 3 billion football fans about the peace and national potential that the Cambodian people have been living in harmony. With a better life and development in all areas.
The World Cup will be held in Cambodia until June 17 before traveling to other countries. During its stay in Cambodia, the trophy was also held at the Moradok Techo Stadium under the strictest security to show its elegant appearance to the eyes of the Cambodian people.
