Senior official of the Ministry of Economy: The insurance sector plays an important role in promoting national economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Silva, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Working Group on Drafting a Policy for the Development of Cambodia's Financial Technology Sector, said that the insurance sub-sector has been playing an important and active role in promoting national economic growth. .
Speaking at the seminar on "The Role of the Insurance Sector and Financial Technology in the Digital Economy of Cambodia" on 15 June 2022, Mr. Ros Silva stated that "for the non-banking financial sector, the insurance sub-sector has been playing a vital role. Important and active in promoting national economic growth. "This sub-sector has made remarkable progress and is developing into a potential sector in the financial industry."
He said that in relation to life insurance activities, the 19-year-old Kovid crisis has shown two trends: 1. Increased awareness of insurance among the general population, especially families with Medium Income.2: Start-up and increase digital service delivery by insurance companies through investment and efforts to increase service efficiency.
At the same time, he said, the growing demand for life insurance is also driven by increasing public awareness through public and private sector outreach efforts, while public awareness And with positive changes, general insurance companies are also increasing their attention with this changing trend.
"Insurance operators have a special function: the ability to absorb the risk that individuals may fall into poverty or misery due to severe financial loss in a country where the insurance market is booming, the resilience of the people's financial safety net," he said. "Like business institutions are strong because there is a lot of protection under the scope of insurance services."
He stressed that the insurance market in Cambodia is still small, the use of insurance services by the people is low and the awareness of the benefits of insurance of the people is still limited.
