6,000-meter road in Poipet city rehabilitated
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Keat Hul, Governor of Poipet City, this morning, June 15, 2022, inspected a 6,000-meter-long dirt road in Tuol Prasat Village, Poipet Sangkat. Flood.
After studying and inspecting, he led the team to complete the bulldozer, compactor, compactor and mix before the rainy season, which was donated by Mr. Ke Kim Yan, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Banteay Meanchey Provincial Assistance and Mrs. Mao Malay Ke Kim Yan.
