Indigenous Communities in Laok Village, O'Chum Commune, O'Chum District, Rattanakiri Province Receive Collective Land Title
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province, this morning, June 15, 2022, handed over the Certificate of Collective Land Ownership to a Kreung Indigenous Community in Laok Village, O'Chum Leu Commune, O'Chum District. . The handover ceremony was also attended by the heads, deputy heads of departments, units and the three armed forces.
Conversation with the indigenous community of the two villages who came to get the land title now, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun considered the collective land title as a very important document as a document representing the whole community property as a document representing rights Of the exclusive ownership of the owner of his land for the actual use of the respective real estate.
At the same time, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun also expressed his appreciation to the Land Registration Team and all stakeholders who worked hard to achieve this task responsibly and transparently and instructed the people of the indigenous communities in both villages. This collective title must be maintained and there must be unity in the community to preserve all land that is registered and used sustainably for future generations.
