(Siem Reap): Siem Reap provincial authorities arrested four gangsters for education while they were carrying knives, causing a surprise to local people.
Lieutenant Colonel Khim Phalla, Police Inspector of Sotnikum District, on June 14, 2022, led a patrol around the area and found a group of 7 gangsters riding 4 motorbikes with knives. Surprise at a point on the red gravel road in Proval village, Tayek commune, Sot Nikum district, Siem Reap province.
According to the Siem Reap Provincial Police, the Inspectorate immediately cooperated with the Tayek Administrative Police Station and the People's Guard to arrest four gangsters and bring them to the inspectorate, where they were between 15 and 22 years old.
After questioning, the gangsters confessed that they had put a machete on the motorcycle they were riding to protect themselves.
In this case, the police cooperated with the village authorities to confiscate one of the haircuts, shave their hair, educate them, make a contract, stop their activities, and allow the guardians to guarantee to return home.
