(Phnom Penh): His Excellency Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia, considers that the allegation that the Belt and Road Initiative is a debt trap is a false accusation.
Speaking to Cambodia-China Friendship Radio during a recent interview, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol praised and praised the Chinese President's Belt and Road Initiative, which is benefiting the world through Develop better connectivity infrastructure, reduce transportation time and costs, and boost the national economy.
He pointed out that the Chinese friend has been helping to build 37 roads, 3,636 kilometers long, of which 30 have been completed, while three more are under construction and four are ready to open construction sites in the near future. In addition, China has been helping to build 12 bridges in Cambodia and is also ready to continue cooperation on a number of major national roads, the construction of a second expressway and a high-speed railway.
"Chinese friend, you do not have to force Cambodia to borrow money to build roads and bridges, we are asking the Chinese friend to let our Chinese friend help us," HE Sun Chanthol praised the belt initiative and The path of the Chinese President, who has been sharing his experience and resources to all countries to implement infrastructure projects to make the world's transportation faster and cheaper.
