According to the Cambodian Cashew Association, this year's cashew exports fell due to weather conditions, resulting in a drop in cashew yields. The Cambodian Cashew Association estimates that this year's cashew yield will drop by 50%.
Ms. In Lay Huot, owner of Chey Sambor Cashew Processing Enterprise, told Fresh News on June 15 that the export of processed cashew nuts of her enterprise was small due to low harvested cashew nuts and declining seed quality. Caused by climate change.
In addition, she also faced some problems, loss of procurement from farmers and market problems, especially the Chinese market, because China's non-Kovid measures have blocked exports to this country. So far, she has collected between 300 and 400 tons from farmers.
She said that as of June, Chey Sambo Cashew Processing Enterprise had exported only one foot of cashew nuts to Japan, amounting to 9 tons, in addition to domestic supply.
She also said that this year some new markets such as Thailand, Africa, Turkey and China have come to study to export cashew nuts, but these markets all offer low prices, which is not equivalent to the cost of production. Can be exported to those markets.
