(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, gave three recommendations to relevant partners to end violence.
This recommendation was made through a speech at the Leaders' Summit on Solutions to End Violence against Children. The three recommendations include:
First, to promote the spirit of unity and strengthen and expand existing bilateral and multilateral cooperation to promote child welfare and child protection, especially to strengthen coordination mechanisms among all stakeholders to share data and Important information to take timely and strict action against all forms of violence against children.
Second, to promote global commitment by mobilizing both financial and non-financial resources to support and ensure the sustainability of the movement to end violence against children within the framework of the United Nations and international organizations, as well as other regions.
Third, accelerate progress towards achieving the goals of the Sustainable Development Goals, especially Goal 16.2: End all forms of violence against children by 2030.
In this speech, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted some of Cambodia's efforts to eliminate violence against children.
In addition, in 2019, Cambodia became a member of the Global Partnership to End Violence Against Children, prioritizing the implementation of alternative child care policies by promoting family-based care instead of care. At childcare facilities, etc.
Samdech Techo said that in 2021, based on the evaluation of the action plan to prevent and respond to violence against children in 2017-2021, Cambodia has been on the right path to prevent violence against children. . Going forward, Cambodia will continue to be more active in ensuring that children are safe everywhere, such as at home, at school and in the community.
In addition, the Royal Government is firmly committed to ensuring that all children will live in an environment conducive to growth and access to nurturing and protection to end violence against children in All forms and achieve Cambodia's commitment in the regional and global framework through the implementation of national plans and policies.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that achieving an end to violence against children also requires global cooperation, especially in the context of the continued spread of Kovid-19, which has hampered the progress of development goals. Sustainability (SDGs) in relation to ending violence against children. Full Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Leaders' Summit on Solutions to End Violence Against Children
(Phnom Penh): At around 8:10 pm on Tuesday, June 14, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a video address at the Leaders' Summit on Solutions to End Violence against Children. .
In his address to the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the organization of the "Leaders' Summit on Solutions to End Violence against Children."
In addition to efforts in individual countries, reaching an end to violence against children as a whole also requires global cooperation, especially in the context of the continuing epidemic of Kovid-19, which has hampered progress. Of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) related to ending violence against children.
Towards an end to global violence against children provides the following three ideas:
First, to promote the spirit of unity and strengthen and expand existing bilateral and multilateral cooperation to promote child welfare and child protection, especially to strengthen coordination mechanisms among all stakeholders to share data and Important information to take timely and strict action against all forms of violence against children
Second, to promote global commitment by mobilizing both financial and non-financial resources to support and ensure the sustainability of the movement to end violence against children within the framework of the United Nations and international organizations, as well as other regions.
Third, accelerate progress towards achieving the goals of the Sustainable Development Goals, especially Goal 16.2: End all forms of violence against children by 2030. General knowledge: Istanbul, a city on two continents?
