Both Cambodia and China continue to deny allegations of covert planning, including concessions to the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLAN) navy using Ream naval bases. Some US policies interpret that Ream naval base will be used as a Chinese naval base in the future.
It should be noted that in 2021, the Biden administration sent Deputy Foreign Minister Wendy Sherman to Phnom Penh to try to restore relations with the Cambodian government. But during the visit, Sherman continued to raise concerns by raising issues ranging from human rights, democracy and the destruction of US infrastructure at Ream Naval Base.
In addition, Sherman warned that Chinese military bases could undermine Cambodia's sovereignty, threaten regional security and adversely affect US-Cambodian relations. Sherman's visit did not improve relations between Cambodia and the United States, but instead made Cambodia turn to China even more.
No country in Asia can abandon China. But more importantly, they still want to have some level of relationship with the United States, either in the economic or security spheres, or both. "That is, the United States should provide other credible alternatives to other countries in the region, including Cambodia, such as economic interests, to prevent them from turning to China."
