The Sri Lankan government said on Tuesday that it had decided to add one more day off per week to civil servants across the country to alleviate their suffering and to encourage them. Growing your own food in the face of the worst financial crisis in decades for Sri Lanka. This is according to the release of Reuters on Tuesday, June 14, 2022.
On Monday night, the Sri Lankan cabinet approved a proposal for public sector workers to receive additional leave every Friday for the next three months, partly due to a shortage of fuel. It makes it difficult for them to travel as well as to encourage them to have time to farm to supply food.
The Sri Lankan government said in a statement: "It seems reasonable to allow government officials to take a day off to engage in agricultural activities at home or elsewhere, which could be a solution. "For food shortages that are expected to occur."
The island nation, which employs about 1 million people in the public sector, is struggling with a shortage of foreign currency, which has resulted in the inability to pay for imports of fuel, food and medicine, while the United Nations (UN) Last week also warned of the emerging humanitarian crisis.
