(Phnom Penh): The location of a cockfighting and apple-growing arena was cracked down by the Russey Keo District Unity Command led by Mr. Ek Khun Doeun, District Governor, detaining 4 people addicted to cockfighting and shooting apples and confiscating chickens 16 heads, as well as some tools for shooting pineapples.
The operation to crack down on the above cockfighting ring took place at 3:00 pm on June 14, 2022, located in a plot of land in Tuol Thnang village, Sangkat Tuol Sangke II, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, during the operation, we detained 4 people and confiscated 16 chickens, 2 cars, 2 tricycles, 9 motorbikes, spraying equipment and Some chairs and chicken coops as well.
After the arrest, the four gambling addicts and the above exhibits were sent to the Russey Keo District Police Inspectorate for legal action.
Private sector requests the Royal Government to extend tax preferences for tourism business until the end of 2022
(Phnom Penh): The private sector has requested the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Economy and Finance to extend the preferential tariffs on tourism until the end of 2022.
Mr. Din Somethearith, President of the Hotel Association, confirmed that the request was made after seeing that the hotel and tourism sector seems to be in a state of ambiguity.
Mr. Din Somethearith told Fresh News on June 14, 2022 that the Royal Government has facilitated a lot, especially the preferential tariffs on tourism until September 2022, but because the situation is still difficult, so the sector The private sector has decided to request the Royal Government to extend the tax concessions until the end of 2022.
Mr. Din Somethearith said that a few days ago, there was a meeting with the participation of representatives of the tourism sector and representatives of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to raise the issue of applying for a preferential tax until the end of 2022. Given that before the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid, Cambodia received about 6.6 million international tourists in 2019, but now, although the situation is better, the level of visitors is still low.
"Of course, there are many favors from the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as tax incentives for tourists and openness for tourists who want to come to Cambodia, however, the sector still receives visitors. "There is still a limit of only one-tenth, so I hope the government will agree to the request of the private sector."
He said that, of course, the tourism sector is not yet very strong, as the hotel industry in Phnom Penh has only 20% of guests, this is a problem in the hotel sector, because only 50% of tourists come to stay. He supports the sector.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Association of Travel Agents of Cambodia, sees that the request for the extension of the private sector preferential tax is something that the Royal Government should consider, because although Cambodia is now fully open to tourists, but the growth of visitors. The number of tourists coming to Cambodia is still limited, although the number of tourists is increasing every week, but the number is not enough.
