Taiwan's Foreign Ministry on Tuesday said that the Taiwan Sea is an international waterway and that the Taipei government supports the passage by US warships. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, June 14, 2022.
On Monday, the Chinese Foreign Ministry claimed that China has sovereignty, sovereignty and jurisdiction over the Taiwan Strait. On Tuesday, Taiwan Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Joanne Ou said China's claim was untrue.
"The Taiwan Strait is an international waterway and subject to the freedom of international law," the Taiwanese spokeswoman told reporters. "We understand and support the contribution of the United States' freedom of navigation mission to promote regional peace and stability," she said.
