Mine Authority asks the Australian Government to continue to support demining work until the last demining in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mines Authority, met with Ms. Kathryn Campbell, Secretary of State of the Australian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade on the partnership and cooperation in the field of mine action. The meeting took place on the afternoon of June 13, 2022 at the Mine Authority.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of Australia for their support of the humanitarian mine action sector in Cambodia since 1994 and for their subsequent support for demining projects since 2006. Provides safe land and saves millions of lives from landmines and explosive remnants of war.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch highlighted the achievements of 30 years since 1992 of the launch of the Humanitarian Mine Action Program in Cambodia under the auspices of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the participation of host countries and development partners, including Australia. An outstanding and strong partner for mine action in Cambodia.
