In the first five months of this year, trade between Cambodia and international trade reached more than 22 billion USD, an increase of 20%
(Phnom Penh): In the first five months of 2022, trade between Cambodia and international markets amounted to 22 billion US dollars, an increase of 19.7% compared to the same period in 2021, amounting to 18.768 million Dollars. This is according to the report from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
According to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, from January to May, Cambodia's trade with international markets amounted to 22.469 million US dollars, an increase of 19.7%, of which exports were worth 9412 million. The dollar rose 34.5% and imports were worth $ 13.057 billion, up 11%.
The garment and footwear industry is Cambodia's highest-earning sector, with exports of garments worth more than $ 3,642 million and footwear worth more than $ 702 million over the past five months, and rubber exports contributing more than 183 million dollars. Million dollars, an increase of 21.6%, machinery and electrical appliances more than 639 million dollars, including some agricultural products.
