Twenty-five shootings a day in the United States have killed at least six people and injured 40 others.
BEIJING, June 12 (Xinhua) - As of 4 pm local time on June 12, according to the statistics of the "Gun Violence Archives", a US non-profit organization, At least six people have been killed and 40 others injured in 25 shootings across the United States.
On June 12, local time, the US Congress issued a statement saying the two parties had already reached an agreement on a new framework for resolving gun violence.
In this regard, US President Biden also said he hoped to sign a draft law on the restriction of gun violence soon to promote gun safety. But how to balance the needs and interests of the parties and the lengthy decision-making process will affect whether the law will be drafted smoothly in the end.
By Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Commentary: Cambodia is a New Model of International Cooperation on the "Belt and Road" Initiative
It should be noted that as an important country for China in promoting the construction of the "Belt and Road" and the "Rectangular Strategy" for Cambodia's national economic development, it is highly consistent with the "Belt and Road" initiative. "Especially connectivity in the field of infrastructure construction.
In addition to accelerating the joint construction of the "Belt and Road" initiative, cooperation in all fields between China and Cambodia has been deepened, and China has invested heavily in its infrastructure. Cambodia, such as roads and bridges, irrigation engineering, power grid projects, ports and airports.
It should be reminded that nine years have passed quickly, along with the "Belt and Road" initiative, which was launched and entered the ninth year, how did Cambodia change and develop? The first is the increase in bilateral trade volume between China and Cambodia.
Over the past two years, Cambodia's agricultural exports to China, such as bananas and rice, have grown rapidly. For example, the volume of Cambodia's banana exports to China in 2020 will reach 270,000 tons, and these figures will reach 320,000 tons in 2021. That is why China maintains its position as the largest export market for Cambodian agricultural products.
The second is the development of tourism. Tourism is one of the four main pillars of Cambodia's economy. From 2014 to 2019, the number of Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia increased from 560,000 to 2.3 million, making China the largest source of tourists in Cambodia.
Phin Vichea Vathana, Consul General of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Guangzhou, China, said that the expressways under construction will play a role in shaping the economic circle of the capital as well as promoting the country's economic development. Length.
Dr. Nak Chendarith, Director of the Cambodian Center for the Research of the 21st Century Maritime Silk Road in Cambodia, said that the "Belt and Road" initiative has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's development strategy, which will help Cambodia achieve its grand goal. By 2030 it will be a middle and high income country and by 2050 it will be a high income country.
Chinese enterprises have been actively involved in the development of Cambodia's electricity, which involves the construction of all types of power plants, such as natural gas, hydropower and solar power. Considering the issue of using clean energy to reduce pollution and climate change, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided that from 2019 onwards, it will convert energy consumption to low carbon.
Whether the mention of the "Belt and Road" initiative or the signing and implementation of a free trade agreement between China and Cambodia is in the common interests of the two countries. But for some time now, Western politicians and some pro-China academics have claimed that China has taken out credit to set up debt traps for countries in Asia and Africa.
While giving interviews to the media on the question, "Cambodia's infrastructure and other development projects are highly dependent on China, will Cambodia fall into China's debt trap in the future?" The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen, replied, "I would like to emphasize that we can not become the only debtor and trapped in China's debt, and China has no intention of trapping debt to Cambodia."
I note that as long as we look at this issue with a little bit of justification and fairness, we can see that this statement has no proof at all.
