(3) Mind: is to pay attention to the purpose and activities with high responsibility.
(4) Vimasa is contemplation, analysis, the use of intellect to achieve the will
Ieng Sotheara explained that companies that follow the "influence" will help businesses succeed:
Will: All jobs must have the will, in short, is your true desire. Example: Want something virtuous.
Diligence: It is a diligent effort, day and night, to try what is good for oneself. Example: We are working somewhere, must be diligent, do not be lazy.
* Mind: is to pay attention to the purpose and activities with high responsibility, do not give up the job easily, have a calm mind to solve problems, have a mind to meditate at work. Example: When we do something, be patient, do not get angry, be mindful all the time
* Vimasa: To do something with a simultaneous evaluation and to do something, to think about the reason why what is being done is difficult and to find a way to solve it. Example: We work somewhere and the place gives us a job to do, we need to immediately think about how to do that easily and quickly.
