Kong Mao, head of production at Haswangshur, a local fertilizer company, told Fresh News that as the days of chemical fertilizers increased, the demand for locally produced organic fertilizers was significantly higher. Production is not yet required.
He said that at present, his company, which produces organic fertilizers for domestic supply, has increased its production to 150 to 160 tons per month and plans to increase production in the future. Despite the high demand, the price did not increase, keeping the price of 1 baht (20 kg) at $ 10 and about $ 500 per ton.
"This opportunity, if there is a handicraft or natural fertilizer factory in the district to expand production or expand the factory even better, which makes his people turn to use organic fertilizer, organic fertilizer, our soil is good and in line with the market purpose," he said. Global because they like organic things.
He said Hasventor organic fertilizers were supplied in Battambang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu and Kampong Cham provinces. Next year, it plans to expand its supply to the whole country and export to Thailand, Laos and Burma. The raw materials used by this company are all local products, such as beef bones, bran, compost, rice husk, etc., which have the benefit of holding water and nutrients to help the soil that can be used in all terrains.
"We increase production according to what we can afford in our production chain because our fertilizers contain a large number of materials imported from Japan, so some of the raw materials are," he said. There is a limit to it, so we design according to the possibilities that we can fix, but we will try our best to keep the price from changing too much.
He observed that the increase in the price of chemical fertilizers has caused some farmers to give up farming, which reduces the use of fertilizers, but if the price of agricultural products increases, it will encourage farmers to increase agricultural production.
Oknha Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, called on local producers or entrepreneurs to invest in local fertilizer production to reduce the import of excessively expensive chemical fertilizers and not to rely on foreign fertilizers.
He called on farmers to return to using natural fertilizers or organic fertilizers produced locally because of lower costs and help local production. In addition, the use of this type of fertilizer also helps the soil, although the results may be slower than chemical fertilizers.
He said that according to research, the use of chemical fertilizers mixed with organic fertilizers has a higher efficiency that farmers should try.
He added, "If there are users, producers increase production." If there are no users who want to increase production, they do not dare because they are afraid of not being able to sell. This is the concern of the traders of the agricultural community who want to increase their production business. Farmers' concern that they will not see much fruit. So we are a little patient because the results are long.
According to experts, the price of imported chemical fertilizers has now risen to more than $ 1,000 per tonne, more than half the price of locally produced organic fertilizers, which are only about $ 500 per tonne.
