Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation in collaboration with Legal Contributors organized a training course on "Third Party Complaints"
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation in collaboration with the Legal Contribution Project under the Second Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) organized a training course on "Third Party Complaints" at the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Center with a total of 61 participants. / People.
In the training course on June 11, 2022, there were 21 people from the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation and 40 people from other institutions, consisting of 6 lawyers, 4 law students, 2 clerk students. 15 legal assistants from different offices, 7 students / staff, 3 Phnom Penh Municipal Court officials, 1 official of the Anti-Corruption Unit, 1 official of the Office of the Council of Ministers and 1 person from other institutions.
It should also be noted that the collaboration between the Cambodian International Cooperation Lawyers Group and the legal contributors under the Memorandum of Understanding came from the initiative of the founding contributors, Ms. Tep Bophal and Mr. Ly Raththy, President of the Cambodian International Cooperation Lawyers Group. The three main purposes are:
* 1: Contribute to the dissemination of the Civil Code, the Code of Civil Procedure and the law related to civil affairs more widely, clearly and effectively in the practice of the legal profession in the field of civil affairs.
* 2: Participate and increase attention in developing the capacity of lawyers and legal assistants in the legal team in the field of civil affairs, especially the preparation of documents in accordance with the prescribed forms and updates on the law and explanations. About the law
* 3: Disseminate the law through standardized and widely disseminated media throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia.
