District Governor and Kamchay Mear District People Ask for Intervention to Raise Fertilizer Prices
(Prey Veng): Kamchay Mear district is a district where up to 90% of the population depends on farming to support their livelihood. Currently, the rising prices of fertilizers make their farms less money-hungry at harvest time.
Residents in Daun Keung commune, Kamchay Mear district, described that the current farming is not very profitable and what is the problem is fertilizer. The man claimed that he had to use about 10 bags of fertilizer per hectare, up to 180,000 riel. When harvested, Eia rice can yield about 5 tons per hectare.
The farmers replied that the use of cow dung could replace cow dung, but now people do not raise cows, so there is no cow dung in the field.
Mr. Soeung Socheat, Governor of Kamchay Mear District, acknowledged the challenges of the people. He said that resolving the issue of fertilizer prices is an issue that is difficult for district authorities to solve.
The district governor requested the Royal Government, especially the relevant ministries and institutions as the staff of the Royal Government to intervene and solve this problem.
"Now our people are complaining about rising fertilizer prices. Rising fertilizer or pesticide prices can only be resolved by the Royal Government. We request the Royal Government to intervene in this matter. ” This is Mr. Soeung Socheat's request.
