This was stated by Ms. Soeng Sor Socheata, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on the occasion of the 73rd Anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 21st Anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day 2022 under the theme Global On "Global Social Protection to End Child Labor" held at the Ministry of Labor on the morning of June 10, 2022.
The Secretary of State added that despite the spread of Kovit-19 disease, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training continues to provide core interventions to children affected and vulnerable to child labor in the target provinces. Implement cash support programs for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age in a total of more than 600,000 poor families to alleviate the burden of improving the lives and nutrition of women and children.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is continuing to eliminate child labor in accordance with the National Action Plan on the Reduction of Child Labor and the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labor (2016-2025), in line with the Global Sustainable Development Goals (2015-2030). .
