Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Provide Ambulances and Medical Support Equipment to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces General Command (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen donated an ambulance and other medical equipment to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) General Command to carry out rescue operations in other accidents. Both within the framework of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the general population.
The handover ceremony of ambulances and medical equipment was held at the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command this morning, Friday, June 10, 2022, presided over by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander and Joint Chiefs of Staff. Of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The ambulance donated to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command is the 50th vehicle donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit through Dr. Chea Ratana, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party to various institutions and units of State.
Dr. Chea Ratana said that this ambulance is part of solving the needs of the army and also helps to rescue the general population. Dr. Chea Ratana claimed that the ambulance had also been handed over to various units of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and will be handed over in the future.
Dr. Chea Ratana considered that the contribution with Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit in this humanitarian activity is to share the fruits of his business to help society. He expressed the view that business growth comes from society, so he must distribute this fruit to society.
During the handover ceremony, on behalf of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) military officers, General Ith Sarath expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for providing ambulances and equipment. Some support the doctor’s actions.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are the General Logistics, always thinking of the army and meeting all the needs of the army.
For General Ith Sarath, the ambulance donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit is an important gift to contribute to the rescue operation of the army, both within the army and the general public in case of emergencies.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that "this donation is a contribution to help the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces use this material to serve in saving lives, not only the army, but also the lives of the people."
General Ith Sarath also highlighted that the ambulance was instructed by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to be used in the rescue work without any political affiliation, that is, all the victims must be rescued.
"According to the recommendations of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, we do not discriminate against any people, we help and we do not consider trends. "How to get our people out of those disasters." This is the additional confirmation of General Ith Sarath.
With the donation of the ambulance, General Ith Sarath instructed the unit that received the ambulance to take care of it properly and always be ready to go to the rescue. In addition, doctors who use this car must learn to use the equipment in the car.
The general also instructed to pay attention to the rescue work without adhering to any trend and also not to take money from the victims.
