Details: An electrical warehouse was completely burnt down, the police used more than 100 cars to control water while a volunteer was seriously injured
(Phnom Penh): An electrical warehouse was engulfed in flames and completely destroyed the equipment in the warehouse, and a volunteer was seriously injured and taken to a Russian hospital.
The fire occurred on the evening of June 9, 2022, at the point of storage of electricity along Street 446, Village 5, Group 34, Sangkat Toul Tum Poung I, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
Colonel Prohm Yorn, director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Fire Prevention and Rescue Office, told Fresh News that after receiving information from residents that a fire was burning in an electrical warehouse in the commune. Toul Tompong I immediately ordered fire trucks at all targets to intervene.
"During this operation, it was difficult for our special forces to intervene in time due to the narrow roads and the rapid flames, which caused the roof of the warehouse to collapse," he said. Make it difficult for our skilled forces to get into the firefight. However, our professional forces are still trying to intervene to prevent the devil from spreading to the homes of the people.
The colonel confirmed that in the case of the above fire, the warehouse of electrical appliances and materials were completely damaged, measuring 15 meters by 25 meters, made of galvanized iron.
