Minister of Education: A good teacher is a person who brings knowledge to practice and constantly improve like an artist
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports and Founder of Education Reform on June 9, 2022, said that good teachers are the ones who apply knowledge and constantly improve. Like an artist.
This statement was made on the occasion that Dr. Hang Chuon Naron participated in the graduation ceremony of the Master of Education in Pedagogical Counseling for the first and second generation pedagogical advisors at the National Institute of Education on June 9, 2022. This.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron stated that "a good teacher as well as a good pedagogical advisor is a person who brings knowledge to practice and constantly improve, which is like an artist, with both science and art."
In addition, Minister Hang Chuon Naron said that the transfer of teaching methods from memorization to technology by students to research and present students, all of which have developed into 21st century skills.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that the education reform is to support the new generation of schools, which is a model of reform, and to participate in this education reform, there are four major factors: teachers, students, schools And parents.
Minister Hang Chuon Naron emphasized that when it comes to changing a school, it is not possible to change alone, but we can create a reform framework with the participation of stakeholders such as: principals, teachers, students, parents. And with the support of the Royal Government.
Dr. Chan Rath, President of the New Generation Pedagogical Research Center and President of the Cambodian Mathematical Society, said that the New Generation Pedagogical Research Center is located on the campus of the National Institute of Education and has started the recruitment and training process for the first generation of pedagogical advisory students. On September 16, 2019.
According to the doctor, in accordance with the principle of knowledge is consistent and the quality is non-negotiable, there are 25 first-generation student teachers, but have met all the conditions and successfully defended the thesis, 17 students, the remaining 8 students. Others allow another year to fill in the gaps.
According to Dr. Chanrath, there were 32 second-generation pedagogical students, plus 8 postponed students, for a total of 40, but only 31 of them successfully met all the requirements and successfully defended their thesis. The remaining nine student teachers are allowed to extend for another year to fill the gaps.
Teacher Chhem Kimsen, a student teacher of the New Generation Pedagogical Center, also shared her successful experience in this training course that in order to be successful, teachers should be: healthy, cultivate love, have self-discipline, know how to manage time And be lazy (lazy to save work, lazy to do later, lazy to wait and lazy to wonder).
Ms. Chhem Kimsen said that the driving force for teachers to come to this course is to be one of the many motivations that can contribute to the development of learning and teaching at the school level of education. Cambodia by providing support to teachers in both teaching techniques (teaching methods, use of technology) and mindfulness.
According to Mr. Sun Somara, Training Coordinator at the New Generation Pedagogical Research Center of the National Institute of Education, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has established the New Generation Pedagogical Research Center to help expand the new generation of schools into investment-oriented public schools. High from the government.
In particular, high quality teachers are required to work there, but the project has also evolved into other target educational institutions, such as the National Institute of Education or the Institute of Pedagogy and the Resource School.
The vision of the Center is to change the character of schools in Cambodia into a supportive mechanism through experienced pedagogical advisors at the school who help train teachers to grow both professionally and ethically, making their school happy. And a place to study.
The role of pedagogical advisors will be more effective if there is a conducive environment from the school management, the cooperation of teachers and all stakeholders. Therefore, I would like to request the Board of Directors, teachers and all stakeholders to open their minds and learn more about the importance of providing pedagogical counseling through our pedagogical advisors to contribute to improving the quality of education in Cambodia. .
