Cambodian-Thai authorities are pushing for the preparation of the Thmar Da border checkpoint in Pursat province against Trat province to become an international border checkpoint in the near future.
(Pursat-Trat): The Pursat Provincial Administration and the Trat Provincial Administration of Thailand on the afternoon of June 9, 2022, held a meeting to discuss economic cooperation, tourism and the promotion of the Thmar Da border checkpoint in Pursat province. Sen Trat Province to become an international border crossing.
The Pursat delegation was led by Mr. Pov Piseth, Deputy Governor of Pursat Province in charge of Border Affairs, while the Trat Provincial Party was led by Mr. Kan Chhay Thep Vorak Chhay and Mr. Na Rong Thepsena, Deputy Governor of Trat Province and the Armed Forces. Experts and other relevant officials of Trat Provincial Administration. The meeting was held at Tbong Krahorm (Phlay Deng) Hall, 4th floor, Trat Provincial Hall, Thailand.
After more than an hour of discussions, the Pursat Provincial Administration and the Trat Provincial Administration agreed to make a report respectfully to their respective governments in pushing for the opening of the Thmor Da-Sen International Gate as soon as possible. To connect the economy and tourism for the benefit of the people of the two countries.
In the above meeting, the Cambodian-Thai side accepted to hold a meeting every three months, which should be held between the two provincial governors to discuss and exchange views on a good way to accelerate together. Open the above international port to be successful.
The two sides also encouraged the relevant authorities to expedite the opening of the four international border crossings as soon as possible.
Amazing! A 1-year-old boy was stabbed to death in a rented room in Por Sen Chey district
The drowning incident happened at 4:10 AM on June 9, 2022 at a rented room in Prey Tea 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the bodies of the victims were Tep Puth Sangva, 1 year and 3 months old, her mother was Da Becky, 22 years old, and her father was Lor Samnang, 19 years old. .
Police said that before the incident, the mother and child were in a rented room alone, while the mother was washing clothes and taking her to the sun, and then went to sleep, leaving the victim daughter to play. The water in the bathroom alone caused her to slip into the water tank.
After a while, the son of another woman, 3 years old, came back from the store, saw his brother planting his head in a bucket of water, and ran to wake his mother to see, then the mother rushed to pull her daughter out. In the water tank. At that time, the little girl did not wake up and was taken to the hospital, but unfortunately, the doctor said that the girl had died of asphyxia.
Local authorities immediately went to the scene to conduct a physical examination and handed over her body to her family for a traditional ceremony.
Commentary: Why does China continue to be the largest export market for Cambodian rice until 2022?
It is noteworthy that China will continue to be the largest export market for Cambodian rice until 2022. What are the reasons why China continues to hold the largest market share for Cambodian rice? Lon Yeng, Secretary General of the Cambodian Rice Federation, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that China has helped buy the most Cambodian rice since 2019. Coming to 2022.
He said that the volume of Cambodian rice exports to China has steadily increased in accordance with the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between the two sides. In 2021, more than 300,000 tons of Cambodian rice was exported to China, or more than 50 percent of total rice exports. By 2022, he expects to reach 400,000 tons, according to the Sixth Memorandum of Understanding, and at a time when exports are growing significantly.
Mr. Lon Yeng also stated that the main reason why China continues to occupy a large share of the Cambodian rice market is due to the high will of the leaders of the two countries, especially the Cambodian leadership, Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chinese President Xi Jinping. Even at the recent meeting in 2022, the two sides further promoted Cambodia's rice exports to China.
Lon Yeng also recalled Samdech Techo Sen's visit to Beijing at the time of the 19th Kovid eruption, a further promotion of the Cambodian rice market for the Chinese people due to a rare and special visit to China. The devastation caused by the Kovid epidemic is a great encouragement to the country and the people of China.
Due to the will of the leaders of the two countries, the relevant ministries in Cambodia and the Chinese side, especially a Chinese state-owned company called COFCO, has tried to promote more Cambodian rice exports to China. The company has also created a special brand for Cambodian rice for sale in China, as it is known that Chinese people like to eat Cambodian fragrant rice because they know the geography of Cambodian rice cultivation, it is grown around the Tonle Sap Lake. Nutritious.
Mr. Lon Yeng added that with the help of the Chinese side, China not only helped to buy more Cambodian rice, but also helped to build agricultural infrastructure for Cambodia, including the construction of irrigation systems. Cultivation is no longer dependent on the sky, but on modern irrigation systems to transfer water from large dams.
"I would also like to thank China, both the Chinese leadership and the people, for helping Cambodia, especially in the construction of some large irrigation infrastructure, to make our rice cultivation more dependent on the sky, more dependent on the irrigation technology. Canals from large dams.
