Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Launches Measures for Provincial Health Units to Disseminate to People to Prevent Some Diseases
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, has issued measures for the units of the Provincial Department of Health and Administration to widely disseminate and intervene to prevent the occurrence of some diseases that are high risk to people's lives if neglected. .
The provincial governor said so on June 9, 2022 in the 36th Ordinary Meeting of the third mandate of the Provincial Council at Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
The provincial governor said that since the provincial council members raised the issue of five types of diseases, there is a high risk to the well-being of the people, including: chickenpox, Kovid 19, blisters, new hepatitis and diseases. Dengue fever.
The governor said that these five diseases have some diseases that people have already gone through, but there are new diseases that we have not gone through, especially new chickenpox that occurs abroad and it can spread. To our country, if we are negligent, there are no preventive measures.
As for the new type of hepatitis, which has not been named yet, it must be informed to the people to be careful. Dengue fever, on the other hand, is a high-risk disease that can affect the elderly and children and should not be underestimated if left untreated.
The provincial governor submitted a number of measures to the provincial administrative health unit to implement, including:
* First, to increase awareness to all health departments in all districts and communes, all referral hospitals and private clinics.
* Second: To promote the spraying of tiger mosquito repellent, make people aware and eliminate all the sources that cause tiger mosquitoes.
At the same time, it is necessary to inform the people if there is dengue fever, it is necessary to hurry to seek treatment at public referral hospitals or health centers to avoid going to private clinics.
