In fact, the Royal Government has given 19 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine to all leaders, civil servants, military forces, doctors, both public and private, journalists, artists, artists, people with weakened immune systems or people in their 60s. This provision is to ensure immunity in the community and no one is affected by the disease.
Please note that the above vaccination campaign starts from 9 to 21 June 2022 at referral hospitals and health centers in various districts in Phnom Penh.
Director General of Taxation urges Chinese companies investing in Cambodia to fulfill tax obligations and register for tax
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, encouraged Chinese investors, both large, medium and small taxpayers, to fulfill their tax obligations in accordance with the law. Tax provisions in force.
The meeting on June 9 was held with the aim of clarifying some points in the implementation of laws and regulations on tax and discuss and solve problems and questions related to tax.
Separately, those who have not yet come to register for tax, Mr. Kong Vibol called on them to participate in tax registration and fulfill their tax obligations in accordance with the laws and regulations on tax in force.
He said that in order to reap the benefits in accordance with the content of the Cambodia-China Agreement on the Avoidance of Double Taxation (DTA), which came into force and was effective from January 1, 2019, enterprises can Apply to the General Department of Taxation, which can be applied in person or online, which is convenient for taxpayers.
The General Department of Taxation and the Chinese Chamber of Commerce (Cambodia) applauded and continued good cooperation in sharing information, further strengthening cooperation, partnership and providing better tax services in order to reduce the maximum Challenges.
As a direction for the implementation of the partnership, the General Department of Taxation-China Chamber of Commerce (Cambodia) will continue to strengthen cooperation and partnership through two regular (regular) meetings per year and extraordinary meetings if necessary. Various.
