In the case of the ammunition bombing east of the CPP headquarters in Svay Dangkum commune, Siem Reap city, the police force arrested two suspects starting from the dispute
(Siem Reap): Police in Siem Reap City on June 7, 2022, arrested two suspects who processed ammunition on the conflicting party on June 3, east of the CPP headquarters in Svay Dangkum commune. Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
According to the report of the Siem Reap City Police Inspectorate, after the incident, Lieutenant Colonel Da Chamroeun, the Siem Reap City Police Inspector, led a criminal investigation force and arrested two suspects who detonated two improvised explosive devices. People.
* First: Name: Seng Sokorn, 18 years old, Occupation: Student, motorcycle repair, Born in Thailand. Currently living in a rented room in Taphul village, Svay Dangkum commune, Siem Reap city / province. * Second name: Ron Darong, alias Hing, 20 years old. Currently living in a rented room in Sala Kamroeuk village, Sangkat Sala Kamroeuk, Siem Reap city / province.
Ron Darong, also known as Hing, was taken to the scene to report the location of the ammunition depot where the assailants had gathered. On June 3, 2022, at 8:00 PM, the day of the incident, the suspect, Seng Sokorn, rode his motorbike to the scene and defused the ammunition, causing an explosion on the road and then driving. The motorcycle escaped alone.
The suspect, Seng Sokorn, told himself that he had detonated a bomb at the location he had been told, and that he had then removed the remaining four rounds of ammunition and threw them on the street. After the arrest, the police confiscated one of the suspects' motorbikes.
The suspects were sent to court by the Office of Case Management for legal action. Encouraging the forces that have worked hard to crack down on crime in the past, Brigadier General Teng Channath, Provincial Police Commissioner through Brigadier General Pheng Chendareth, Deputy Commissioner also donated 1,000,000 Riels.
