(Phnom Penh): Mr. The Chhun Hak, Director General of the General Department of Gender Equality and Economic Development of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, said that relieving the burden as well as easing the housework of women will help make women go out of business fully. Find a wider business of women entrepreneurs.
Mr. Te Chhun Hak made the remarks at the launch of "In Her Hands" magazine, organized by the United States Agency for International Development (USAID) and Pak Cambodia on June 7, 2022.
Mr. Te Chhun Hak said, "In order for women to have full potential to participate in business, it is necessary to participate in relieving the burdens of women The more extensive the women's business, the better. ”
He said that helping women to get investment capital, have a market to do business, have digital knowledge and help solve the burden of household chores, the step into women's business will grow.
Please be informed that "In Her Hand" is a magazine that provides women entrepreneurs in Cambodia with tools to build their business. By providing key resources and case studies, the magazine acts as a guide on how entrepreneurs can cope with the challenges they face in business, such as how to register with the National Social Security Fund.
The magazine is available in Khmer and English and details the key steps needed to transform a small informal business into a legitimate enterprise with high growth potential and legal protection.
"The United States Agency for International Development (USAID) strongly supports the participation of women and the economy of women, and access to information is important," said Han Wen, Acting Director of the United States Agency for International Development in Cambodia. For participation. This magazine will provide Cambodian women entrepreneurs with the information they need to start and expand their business. ”
"This magazine supports women entrepreneurs in making their dream business a reality," said Sabin Youngers, Country Director of PAC Cambodia. "This magazine presents real-life stories of women entrepreneurs about challenges and provides practical steps to address issues so that women entrepreneurs can solve them."
