The Cambodian Women's Association of the Republic of Korea issues a statement praising the free, fair and transparent election process in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): As an international observer on the Commune / Sangkat Council election process of the fifth mandate, the Cambodian Women's Association of the Republic of Korea highly appreciates and appreciates the free, fair and transparent election process.
"We do not see any signs of intimidation or violence in any of the polling stations we observed during this election, and voters are free and happy to vote. Lead their respective communes. ” This is confirmed in the statement of the Cambodian Women's Association in the Republic of Korea.
The Cambodian Women's Association of the Republic of Korea noted that while observing the election process, its members also carefully examined the process and environment of the election campaign, voting, vote counting and the use of digital technology for the election. Find names and polling stations easily and quickly.
In addition, the election process has been actively involved in the observation of the relevant political party agencies, which has been well conducted, as well as the active and free participation that demonstrates the aging and credibility of The process of democratization in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In the statement, the Cambodian Women's Association of the Republic of Korea commended the National Election Committee for its efforts in organizing the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election in a smooth, fair, and transparent manner in accordance with the principles of democracy. Liberal, multi-party.
Through this statement, the Cambodian Women's Association of the Republic of Korea congratulates the Cambodian people on their efforts to maintain peace and promote democracy through elections to maintain peace and prosperity.
The association is confident that democracy in Cambodia will continue to grow and that the Cambodian people will be able to take advantage of this democratic process. Six Associations in Australia and New Zealand Release Statement on Cambodia's Commune / Sangkat Council Election Process as a Model for Regional Countries
(Phnom Penh): Six associations based in Australia and New Zealand, which have sent their representatives to observe the conduct of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election in Cambodia, have issued a statement evaluating That the process of commune council elections in Cambodia is a model for countries in the region.
The associations commended and highly commended the National Election Committee (NEC) for its efforts to ensure that the election process went smoothly and in a good environment, both during the election campaign and without election day. Any violence or threat.
The Association commends the Royal Government of Cambodia for its commitment to upholding the Cambodian Constitution and Law in order to maintain democracy in Cambodia through regular and secure elections. Six associations based in Australia and New Zealand also joined in celebrating the glorious victory of all Cambodians who have contributed to the preservation and strengthening of democracy in Cambodia.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh to Attend the 19th Asia Security Summit on June 10-12 in Singapore
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, will lead a high-level delegation of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to attend the 19th Asia Security Summit (Sangeilla Dialogue) to be held on December 10-12. June 2022 in Singapore at the invitation of Dr. John Chipman, Director General and Chief Executive Officer of the International Institute for Strategic Studies.
A press release from the Ministry of National Defense, obtained by Fresh News on June 7, 2022, states that the Summit for 2022 will have seven plenary sessions on the following topics:
On the occasion of attending the 19th Asia Security Summit, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh will deliver a meaningful statement at the Fourth Plenary Session on "Military Modernization and New Defense Capabilities" On the challenges posed by the rapid military development in the region and the functions that these new capabilities can play in balancing regional stability.
As the chair of the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting (ADMM) and related meetings in 2022, Samdech Picheay Sena will also highlight Cambodia's position in the efforts to promote the role and unity of ASEAN together to address security challenges. According to the theme of the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting "Solidarity for Harmonious Security".
In addition to attending the summit, Samdech Pich Sena will also hold bilateral meetings with the defense ministers of the countries of Australia, China, Singapore and the United States, as well as receive courtesy calls from key dignitaries. Including the director of the International Committee of the Red Cross in the Asia-Pacific region.
