(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, confirmed to the new OHCHOR Representative in Cambodia that the 5th2220 Commune / Sangkat Council Election Process, which has just been completed, was free and fair. The party gives people the right to choose the party they love, which shows their democracy and their true will.
Mr. Keo Remy made this remark after a working meeting between him and Ms. Ruel Adhal Hach, Representative in Cambodia, the Office of the new United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (OHCHOR) on the morning of the 7th. This June 2022.
Mr. Keo Remy stated: “In the Human Rights Committee, we applaud the Commune / Sangkat Council election, which has a multi-party system as a choice that gives the people the right to choose whichever party they choose. "Loving through trust, choosing local leaders to serve the interests of the local people is a good thing."
According to Mr. Keo Remy, this election was attended by many party representatives and other parties won seats at the local level, making the people have their own representatives, both the CPP and other parties are free. A multi-party that offers choices to the people.
"And voting voluntarily is great. It is better to have a party and to be forced to vote for a party that you do not like and still vote for, so that the Human Rights Committee understands that civil rights, political rights are guaranteed. In the election every five years. This is an additional statement of Mr. Keo Remy.
In addition, he added that for the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022, there are national and international observers, representatives of political parties, journalists, civil society organizations, which is an important point in the election process. Go smoothly and correctly.
According to Mr. Keo Remy, the new OHCHOR representative will cooperate with the Human Rights Committee to focus on the 2023 parliamentary election.
