(Phnom Penh): National observers who participated in observing and monitoring the election process of Commune / Sangkat Councils of the 5th mandate saw that it was not possible to rig the ballots or exchange ballots at polling stations.
In a press conference on the results of the election observation held on Monday afternoon, June 6, 2022, Mr. Nong Buntheng said that he had deployed members from his organization to observe the election process at the polling stations. Some are even permanent observers.
Mr. Nong Buntheng described that as a permanent observer, he and his members had been following the June 5 election process very closely since the polling station, polling station, and counting process. And ballot storage.
Observers who focus on the accuracy of the electoral process and are the eyes and ears of the electorate have praised the conduct of the election as transparent, free and fair. He noted that people went to the polls in large numbers and went to the polls with happy faces. He said through the smiles on the faces of the voters, it shows that the voters are happy with the election and vote without any emotional pressure or coercion.
"It is very free and fair," said Nong Buntheng. Why? When I observe without going out even for a moment. "We participated in counting one ballot at a time until there was an agreement to show it to all the observers, and the party representatives agreed to the final count."
Mr. Nong Bun added, "I am tired of accusing each other of us Khmers as well. I always knew that the accusation was correct? It should not be, it is not possible, because in our eyes a lot of 4 to 5 observers there, including 6 other NEC officials who work regardless of party affiliation, how to make his work successful "Smoothly."
