(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 6, 2022, the Secretariat of the Permanent Security Command for Elections (CEC) in collaboration with the Press and Quick Reaction Unit of the Office of the Council of Ministers released a video. 12 minutes under the title: "Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate Reflects the Maturity of Multiparty Liberal Democracy in the Kingdom of Cambodia."
Watch the video: TOP NEWS: ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly: No Threat to the People in the Commune / Sangkat Council Election Process in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In a statement issued on June 6, 2022, the delegates of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) affirmed that in the process of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 in Cambodia, which has just ended. This is not an act of intimidation or violence.
AIPA added that based on the information received before and during the election, each delegate understood that the election procedure was conducted in accordance with national law and an effective technique. Commune / Sangkat elections were successfully concluded in a peaceful and participatory atmosphere, as well as demonstrating the integrity and gentleness of the electorate.
The ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly also saw that the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council elections in Cambodia proceeded peacefully and smoothly in a free, fair and transparent environment, in which all political parties freely participated in the proceedings. Vote completely without interruption. All parties have equal opportunities and rights before the law, which proves that the democratic process should be satisfactory in Cambodia.
A transparent system has been put in place to ensure that observers from all political parties, national and international NGOs can closely monitor the entire electoral process. The vote count was conducted with the use of an effective mechanism under the watchful eye of observers.
Delegates observed that in the offices they visited, there were capable staff standing to facilitate voters. All polling stations are equipped with essential materials, including voter lists, ballot papers, ink seals and empty ballot boxes certified by the first voter at each polling station.
In addition, AIPA stated that the Cambodian authorities have fully fulfilled their duty to ensure the safety and security of all participants during the election process, including international observers at the site. The AIPA delegation's observation supports the holding of free, fair and regular multi-party elections as a democratic means by which all public officials should practice at the regional and national levels.
Delegates conclude that the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council election process was successful and allowed the Cambodian people to exercise their civil and political rights through a general, secret ballot with the application of national and international law. With a peaceful, efficient and transparent election process and a high turnout, AIPA delegates congratulate the Cambodian people on this success.
Please be informed that at the invitation of the National Election Committee (NEC) through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Office of the Secretary General of the National Assembly of Cambodia, the delegation of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA), which includes AIPA members Four members and one representative from the AIPA Secretariat participated as election observers in Cambodia.
