"For me, the observers in Kep province, this kind of intimidation for me seems to be non-existent, because in the NEC law, there is security, there is an observer, and the observers have the right ethics, so no," he said. What is intimidation, people go to the polls, laugh and have fun. "There is no clear argument for this."
