National Bank of Cambodia officially launches Housing Price Index
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the National Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning on June 6, 2022 officially launched the Housing Price Index.
According to Dr. Chea Serey, the introduction of the Housing Price Index will make an important contribution to monitoring, evaluating and formulating development policies as well as measures to minimize risks in order to maintain macroeconomic stability.
Dr. Chea Serey continued that the development of the housing sector is considered to contribute to improving the quality of life and daily life of the people. At the same time, housing development not only contributes to meeting basic needs, but also plays an important role and is an essential vehicle for wealth accumulation through investment in construction and home ownership.
In particular, before the outbreak of the Kovid 19 health crisis in Cambodia, the construction and real estate sectors became an important sector to boost Cambodia's economic growth in almost 10 years before the Kovid 19 crisis, the average economic growth rate of about 7%, of which 2% From the construction and real estate sector and absorbed nearly 500,000 workers to work in this sector, according to the results of the 2019 census.
She said that although the housing sector has played an important role in the social and economic sectors, it is also a source of instability and economic crisis.
