(Phnom Penh): The election process of Commune / Sangkat Council of the 5th mandate on Sunday, June 05, 2022 has run under a good atmosphere. From 7 am, when the polling stations opened, it was observed that in all 23,602 polling stations nationwide, a significant number of people went to the polls.
Voting went fast. Data from the National Election Committee show that as of 11 a.m., more than 56 percent of the population, or more than 5 million people, had already cast their ballots.
Throughout the election process this morning, it was observed that all polling stations were operating in a good environment, maintaining order and giving high confidence to the people who went to the polls. People who went to the polls were observed with happy smiles, a sign of satisfaction and joy for the election.
Looking back on social media, it can be seen that people who went to the polls took pictures of themselves dipping their hands in ink to show their participation in the election, accompanied by a message calling for people to go to the polls.
Apart from the polling stations on the streets in Phnom Penh, they also observed heavy traffic and normal traffic. Businesses are still going on as usual, people returning from the election are also meeting and chatting or doing their jobs regularly.
These pictures show that the people are more confident and confident in the election process in Cambodia, as opposed to the previous election. In previous elections, people were always worried about the changing situation in society, especially fear of any chaos after the election. That concern has led some people to buy food, leading to inflation in the market.
The view of the Commune / Sangkat Council elections in Cambodia in the fifth mandate shows that there is a clearer understanding of the democratic process in Cambodia, or in other words, the democratic process is deeper and stronger in Cambodian society. The people understand that the election is just a process of electing a leader according to the will of the people, not a battle for power.
Cambodia is a country that used to use force to seize power in the past and bring about the most devastating tragedy. The political shift from a change of leadership from a weapon to the voice of the people in a democracy is a source of pride for the Cambodian nation.
May the results of the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election be accepted by all political parties and become the applause of all citizens. May the foundations of democracy in Cambodia be stronger as a cool shade for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
