The Commune / Sangkat Council Election is a general election in which the general Cambodian population aged 18 and over is included in the official voter list of the Commune / Sangkat in which they wish to vote. Voters must bring a valid Khmer Nationality Identity Card (OKK) or Voting ID (ID) if the voter does not have an AEC.
Voters are required to line up in front of the polling station to enter the polls in order. Separately, monks, the elderly, pregnant women, women with small children, the disabled and the sick are given priority.
Voting ends at 3:00 pm today, but if there are still voters in the polling station or standing in line or inside the polling station, they must be allowed to vote. The Chief of the Polling Station may declare the end of the election at his / her polling station before 3:00 pm if all the voters on the polling station's voter list have cast their ballots.
