Understand Commune / Sangkat Council Elections
(Phnom Penh): This Sunday, June 05, 2022, from 7 am to 3 pm is the time when the polling station is open for Commune / Sangkat Council elections.
What is Commune / Sangkat Council Election?
Commune / Sangkat Council Election is a democratic process at the sub-national level organized by the Royal Government of Cambodia to give people the opportunity to exercise their power to elect Commune / Sangkat Chiefs and Commune / Sangkat Councils as locomotives. Lead in the commune / sangkat where they live.
Commune / Sangkat council elections are the second major election after the National Assembly election. Commune / Sangkat councils are local leaders who receive power from the Royal Government. Each Commune / Sangkat Council has 5 to 11 members, which is proportional to the population in each Commune / Sangkat. Commune / Sangkat councils are chaired by a chairman elected from the party that receives the most popular votes.
The establishment of Commune / Sangkat Councils through universal suffrage is a major political turning point in Cambodia. The important thing is that the local authority is the direct leader and close to the people who used to be appointed by the upper level. However, for 4 terms, the Commune / Sangkat Council is directly elected by the people.
Through this election, commune / sangkat officials must show more responsibility to the people, otherwise they will be ousted by the people through the ballot every five years.
Commune / Sangkat council elections are held universally, as are parliamentary elections. This election was first held in 2002, counting as the first mandate. Since 2002, Commune / Sangkat Council elections have been held regularly every five years.
Commune / Sangkat Council candidates who are running for election are selected from political parties that have registered to vote with the National Election Committee (NEC). Commune / Sangkat Council candidates are also registered with the NEC.
According to NEC data, in the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election, 17 political parties registered to contest, with a total of 86,092 Commune / Sangkat Council candidates, 27,813 of whom were women. People.
Commune / Sangkat council elections are held every five years, and it is very important that people do not miss them. In order to participate in the election, citizens must have their names on the voter list and have a Cambodian identity card or other identification document for the election.
