The following are 9 guidelines for educating Cambodians about Commune / Sangkat Council elections:
* First, in order to vote, citizens must have their names on the voter list and have a Cambodian identity card or other identification document to vote.
* Second, we need to know the number, our name, the code and the location of the polling station as stated in the voter registration receipt and in the published voter list or in the voter information card.
* Third: We need to prepare the time and identity card of Khmer nationality or identification documents for the election to use on election day.
* Fourth: We can vote for any political party we like without any threat, intimidation or coercion.
* Sixth: Each voter has the right to vote only once and only once, to go to the polling station in person with his / her name on the voter list and bring with him / her Khmer identity card or identification document to use. Elections.
* 7th: Khmer citizens who have already registered and are on the voter list but did not go to the polls lose their right to participate in the development of the commune and society.
* Eighth: In order to have competent and wise commune councils, we must all participate in free, fair and just democratic elections, directly and secretly.
9th: Villages, communes, sangkats are safe and can be developed depending on the competent and wise commune councils.
