Dubai: Saudi Arabia and other OPEC members may increase oil production to offset declining Russian oil output, a measure that could ease rising oil prices and rising inflation. According to Reuters.
Two sources from the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC +) told Reuters that the group was working to supplement Russia's declining oil output as Russia's oil production fell by about 1 million barrels a year. One day (bpd) due to Western sanctions on Moscow for invading Ukraine.
Other sources make it clear that OPEC + could accelerate output growth to 650,000 barrels a day in July and August, up from the original plan of 432,000 barrels. One day planned for July, August and September.
