(Phnom Penh): "Rainbow to Tomorrow" is a song written to highlight the deep emotions of the friendship between a famous Japanese singer and the people of Cambodia during this singer Visited Cambodia since Cambodia was in poverty due to the civil war crisis.
The song "Rainbow to Tomorrow" was prepared by the famous Japanese singer and actress Minami Yuko and her team, especially for the "Kizuna Festival 2022" and the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Japan and Cambodia in 2023.
The meaning of the song shows her help to create a smile and light of life for the orphans, which shows the deep sympathy and enthusiasm of the Japanese people for the people of Cambodia. The meaning of the song evokes the strong spirit of the people of Japan in helping the Cambodian people to move towards a hope, which is the common desire of the people of Cambodia and the people of Japan.
In her respectful message to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Ms. Mina Minuyoko expressed her surprise to hear Prime Minister Hun Sen listen to this song.
"I am very excited to receive this valuable letter directly from the Prime Minister," she said. I am very honored. ”
She stated that she had visited Cambodia twice in 1989 and 2013, and in 1989 there was no Japanese embassy in Phnom Penh. At that time, she went to primary schools, orphanages, hospitals, etc. in Cambodia .... She learned a lot and felt different.
Ms. Mina Minoyoko highlighted that after returning to Cambodia in 2013, she intends to continue to have close relations with Cambodia to become stronger. Starting from this intention, she also wrote this song.
She hopes that the Cambodian people have listened to this song. In 2023, the 70th anniversary of Cambodia-Japan relations, Mina Yoko is expected to return to Cambodia and sing "Rainbow to Tomorrow".
