(Prey Veng): Under the development policy between the national and local levels, Kamchay Mear district, a district in Prey Veng province, has achieved remarkable development. Achievements Roads, bridges, schools, temples, hospitals are being built to meet the needs of the people. The roads in the communes, which used to be dirt roads, have become concrete or red gravel roads, helping people to travel and transport their crops better.
Mr. Soeung Socheat, Governor of Kamchay Mear District, said that Kamchay Mear District has 8 communes, 129 villages and a population of more than 100,000 people, and almost 90% of the population is engaged in agriculture.
The district governor from the Cambodian People's Party said that Kamchay Mear district was originally considered a remote district and was not very developed. However, under the National Development Policy of the Royal Government from the Cambodian People's Party, National Road No. 8 was built, which is an important road network for economic integration between Kamchay Mear district to other districts in Prey Veng province, as well as to other areas.
In addition to the national policy, the Royal Government's local development policy, together with the national working group to help Kamchay Mear district, headed by Mr. Steng Sokhom, also helped to develop Kamchay Mear district. Mr. Soeung Socheat said that Kamchay Mear district, the hometown of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, received high attention from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Prey Veng Provincial Assistance Team.
According to Mr. Soeung Socheat, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng has turned many villages in the village from a dirt road to a concrete road to facilitate travel and transport agricultural products, provide clean water system for people to use. Help equip health facilities in health centers, build schools and temples. All those achievements meet the urgent needs of the people in Kamchay Mear district.
Achievements and progress in Kamchay Mear district are also recognized by the people living in this district. Man Savun, a 64-year-old resident of Krabao Chuor village, Krabao commune, Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, said his village has seen a lot of growth in recent years. Many concrete roads have been built to facilitate people's travel, and people's lives have also improved.
The CPP's focus on developing and improving the lives of the people has made Mr. Man Savun very satisfied with this political party. Mr. Man Savun said that since he was born, especially after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, he saw that only the Cambodian People's Party paid high attention to national development and improving the lives of the people. Better.
On June 05, 2022, Cambodia will hold Commune / Sangkat Council elections to elect locomotives in communes, which are important operators in developing and improving the lives of local people.
Although Krabao Chuor village, Krabao commune, his hometown, is now remarkably developed, Mr. Man Savun still wants a commune chief who pays close attention to the lives of the people and provides services quickly. And there is no discrimination.
Responding to the request of the above people, Mr. Sou Phuong, 71 years old, the candidate for Krabao commune chief from the Cambodian People's Party, which has controlled the commune for two terms, said that if he received the trust from He will continue to make more efforts to provide services to the people. In particular, seek funding to build more concrete roads in the commune.
