Ministry of National Defense to host 19th ASEAN Regional Political Security Conference tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): Subcommittee on Content and Documents of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to Host the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings 2022 to Organize the 19th ASEAN Regional Political Security Conference (19th ASPC) On June 3, 2022, through a video system under the theme "Solidarity for Security, Harmony".
A press release obtained by Fresh News states that the high-level regional conference will be chaired by General Nem Sovath, Special Adviser to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense, Director General of the Ministry of National Defense's Political and Foreign Affairs Department. The participation of senior officials in the field of security and defense policy of the 27 ASEAN member countries, including representatives of the ASEAN Secretariat.
During the conference, the ASEAN Regional Forum will exchange views on regional and international issues, focusing on:
* (1): The evolution of the regional and international security and defense situation * (2): The search for measures to promote regional defense cooperation after the 19-year-old KV and * (3): the promotion of confidence-building measures and Strengthening solidarity and defense cooperation among ASEAN Regional Forum members towards a harmonious security.
The ASEAN Regional Political Security Conference is an important forum for high-level dialogues on regional and international security and defense issues, and to promote mutual trust and understanding among the participating countries in order to strengthen peace, stability and security. Sustainable local security.
The hosting of the 19th ASEAN Regional Political Security Conference confirms the commitment of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to host the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting (ADMM) and related meetings in 2022 to promote ASEAN unity, jointly address regional security challenges, both now and in the future, in line with the theme "Unity for Harmonious Security."
