The Senior Minister further stated that these achievements were achieved because Cambodia has a clear structure to manage the field of mine action from the national level to the sub-national level under the leadership of the Mine Authority, which is the staff of the Royal Government and the public institution of the state to manage. Supervise, lead and coordinate activities throughout the country.
He added that now, in addition to the support from donor countries and development partners, the mine action sector is beginning to receive the attention and support of the private sector and philanthropists who are doing business in Cambodia. Participate in the implementation of the Mine Action Village Mechanism of the Mine Authority according to its resources.
Paul Clements said he had been living in Cambodia since 2008 and for the past 14 years he was pleased and appreciative of the Royal Government of Cambodia's leadership in ensuring political peace and stability. Provides a lot of opportunities and favorable to investors, especially respect for the culture, traditions and friendliness of the Cambodian people.
