APSARA Authority warns of a fine of 400,000 Riels on tourists who violate the six bans at the Angkor Botanical Garden
(Siem Reap): Officials of APSARA Authority have warned of a fine of 400,000 Riels for both national and international tourists who do not follow the instructions or violate the six prohibitions at the plant park to maintain sustainability, environment, hygiene and cleanliness in the park This.
Meak Bora, manager of the Angkor Botanical Garden of the APSARA Authority, said that in order to maintain sustainable hygiene in the Angkor Botanic Garden resort, the APSARA Authority has imposed six bans, with severe fines of up to 40 Ten thousand riels.
Those bans include:
He added that the six-point ban is already on the ticket and there are staff to guide tourists to understand more. He added that these bans to make this resort more attractive to tourists after they visit Angkor Wat or other ancient temples, because the Angkor Botanical Garden is near Angkor.
This popular resort is located along the road to Angkor Wat in Kork Chak, Siem Reap on an area of more than 15 hectares with more than 500 species of plants in the garden. After being opened to the public free of charge since May 19, 2022, so far, more than 20,000 tourists have visited the plant.
This Angkor Botanical Garden is very special in preserving important Khmer plants, especially plants that can be used as a medicine. In addition to growing herbs as an important concept, it is also important to help the environment process climate change by providing shade and oxygen to the respiratory system.
At the same time, the initiative to establish the Angkor Botanical Garden is also to help climate change in the Angkor area, promoting the environment and promoting public health and tourists.
DPM Chea Sophara Leads a Delegation to Inspect Areas 2 and 3 of the Tonle Sap Lake in Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Following an order from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, this morning, June 1, 2022, led an inter-ministerial delegation to inspect Land area 2 and area 3 of Tonle Sap Lake is located in Kampong Chhnang province after visiting Battambang, Pursat province on 27 and 28 May.
On May 27, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced to cut the Tonle Sap Lake Conservation Land from Zone 3 and Zone 2 to the people who have actually enjoyed 10 years or more or less than 10 years for the land. Not flooded forest land and shallow land can not be restored. Samdech also ordered Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara to inspect the distribution of land to people in these areas.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also met with the people who live and enjoy the land.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has divided the Tonle Sap Lake land into three areas to facilitate management. Zone 3 is land that can not be enjoyed and can not be owned, Zone 2 is land that can be enjoyed but can not be owned and Zone 1 is land that can be enjoyed and can be Owners can, too.
In a special message on Tonle Sap Lake land management on May 27, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the management of the Tonle Sap Lake must take into account two main tasks: conservation and consideration for living and enjoyment. Of the people. Samdech Techo would like to confirm that for the land that people have enjoyed and lived for a long time, even in the conservation area as zone 2 and zone 3 must be cut off to the people.
