(Phnom Penh): Nearly 200 French companies and businesses will seek investment opportunities and markets in Cambodia to boost exports, imports and expand trade between the two countries as French business experts prepare for the "French-Cambodian Business Forum" For the first time in the middle of this month.
He added that Cambodia is a developing country, so there are many potential sectors that investors are interested in. Those sectors include tourism and agriculture, which France needs to strengthen and participate in further development. At the same time, despite the growth of the textile, garment and footwear sector, it is still an important sector that French investors are looking at.
"The Franco-Cambodian Business Forum is an opportunity for us to look at potential markets, and when the French side comes and he listens to us, that is when we can find other markets and business opportunities," he said. That can work together between Cambodian and French business.
