He said that most of the goods that Cambodia exports to France are garments, clothes, shoes and rice, so he wants to have other products exported to the French market.
According to data from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, in the first four months of 2022, the trade volume between Cambodia and France was more than 170 million US dollars, of which Cambodia exported more than 133 million US dollars to France. 37.4% and France imported more than $ 43 million to Cambodia, an increase of 59.3%.
The Thai government, along with Vietnam, plans to reach an agreement between the world's second and third largest rice exporters to increase their bargaining power and help reduce growth, Reuters reported on Friday. Production costs.
Vietnam has not yet confirmed whether the plan is being discussed.
His comments were similar to those of the president of the Vietnam Food Association, who last week said that raising prices at a time of global food uncertainty would be unreasonable.
The Thai and Vietnamese Ministries of Agriculture did not immediately respond to a request for comment by Reuters on Monday.
India, the world's largest exporter of rice, supplies about 40 percent of the world's supply, and rice prices fell to a five-year low last week as the Indian rupee weakened and supply Large among rice exporters. India has no plans to restrict rice exports, Indian officials said last week.
India's 5% broken white rice is $ 50 cheaper per tonne than Vietnamese rice and $ 100 cheaper than Thailand's, rice traders said Monday. In recent years, Vietnam has imported some Indian rice for use in beer and animal feed.
Vietnam and Thailand have lost market share and will have to cut prices to regain market share, he added.
A trader in Ho Chi Minh City said the formation of a group of rice exporters was unlikely to give a "much different view" on the issue and because the two countries were not the largest exporters.
"If India curbs exports, prices will rise without the need for a rice group between Thailand and Vietnam," he said.
Vietnam and Thailand account for about 10 percent of global rice production and about 26 percent of global rice exports, Reuters reported, citing data from the US Department of Agriculture.
China announces measures to support economy affected by Kovid-19 (Video inside) (Beijing): China's Cabinet on Tuesday announced a package of 33 measures covering fiscal policy, finance, investment And industrial policies to revive the economy affected by epidemics. According to a report by Reuters.
The stimulus package underscores Beijing's shift to growth following the introduction of measures to prevent Kovid-19, which has hit the economy and threatened Beijing's 5.5 percent growth target for this year.
To restore investment and reuse, the Chinese government has ordered local governments not to extend the ban on car purchases, and those already blocked should increase their quotas, Reuters reported. Car ownership gradually returned.
China's Ministry of Finance also said on Tuesday that it would halve the tax on the purchase of minivans.
China will promote the healthy development of flash companies operating, which is expected to play a role in maintaining job stability, the State Council said.
The company, which operates a fleet of operations, was also encouraged to work in areas such as cloud computing, artificial intelligence and blockchain technology, the latest signs that China is easing its grip on the state, the council said. Crack down on e-commerce and big tech companies.
The package shows that China will also expand private investment, accelerate infrastructure construction and boost the purchase of cars and home appliances to stabilize investment.
In the area of monetary and financial policy, China will increase the efficiency of financing through capital markets by supporting local companies to register in Hong Kong and promoting overseas listings by qualified fleet operators. . According to Reuters.
